<edge source="d336f173-6cc0-4c2f-8c9a-c2ab9ab132f3" target="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 death benefit applies if the insured passes away during the 20-year policy term. This ensures that the benefit is tied to the lifespan of the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORAL_SCOPE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d336f173-6cc0-4c2f-8c9a-c2ab9ab132f3" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit of $300,000 defines the payout if the insured dies during the term, whereas the annual premium of $1,620 represents the cost to maintain coverage. They are separate components of the policy’s structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d336f173-6cc0-4c2f-8c9a-c2ab9ab132f3" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is independent of the payment schedule; it remains fixed regardless of whether premiums are paid annually or otherwise.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d336f173-6cc0-4c2f-8c9a-c2ab9ab132f3" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit of $300,000 applies only if the insured dies during the term. This outcome is unrelated to the return of premium, which occurs solely upon surviving the entire term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d336f173-6cc0-4c2f-8c9a-c2ab9ab132f3" target="1c93bad2-a530-4021-9ae6-510c48444611">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 death benefit is payable to the primary beneficiary, Carlos Roberto Martinez, if Nicole Christine Martinez passes away during the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">PAYABLE_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d336f173-6cc0-4c2f-8c9a-c2ab9ab132f3" target="444a4f43-1071-49e4-ad9e-358f2bf54de9">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is specified independently of the identity of the spouse listed as the primary beneficiary. This detail provides clarity about payout magnitude but does not rely on knowing who the husband is.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d336f173-6cc0-4c2f-8c9a-c2ab9ab132f3" target="47224cc0-60b9-43a5-887d-8ab3626989c4">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 death benefit provides the financial foundation for what Carlos Roberto Martinez receives upon Nicole’s passing. As the designated primary beneficiary, he is entitled to the full amount specified by the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d336f173-6cc0-4c2f-8c9a-c2ab9ab132f3" target="f0614009-4ad3-4925-af16-fcdd6c7ce2a0">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 death benefit would be payable to the primary beneficiary, Carlos Roberto Martinez, unless he predeceases Nicole, in which case the contingent beneficiary, Sofia Isabella Martinez, would receive it.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
