  <data key="d3">The 20-year term specifies how long coverage remains active; it is unaffected by Nicole’s "Preferred Plus" rating, which instead impacts premium calculation rather than longevity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="d336f173-6cc0-4c2f-8c9a-c2ab9ab132f3">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the period during which the $300,000 death benefit is available to beneficiaries. Without this timeframe, the scope of when the benefit triggers would be undefined.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term establishes the policy's duration, which directly determines its termination date of September 15, 2044.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s 20-year term defines its duration, but it does not influence the fixed annual premium of $1,620, which is set independently based on underwriting factors.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year policy term establishes the time frame during which annual premiums are due, making the annual payment schedule consistent with the overall duration of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="1c93bad2-a530-4021-9ae6-510c48444611">
  <data key="d3">The policy's 20-year term defines its duration but does not influence who the primary beneficiary is. Beneficiary designation remains independent of the policy’s length.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year policy term sets the timeframe during which coverage is active; only by surviving this full duration does the policyholder qualify for the return of $32,400 in premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="444a4f43-1071-49e4-ad9e-358f2bf54de9">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s 20-year term defines its duration but does not affect the identification of Carlos Roberto Martinez as the spouse. This factual detail supports contextual completeness without direct causal or sequential dependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="f0614009-4ad3-4925-af16-fcdd6c7ce2a0">
  <data key="d3">The policy's 20-year term defines its duration but provides no direct insight into beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="47224cc0-60b9-43a5-887d-8ab3626989c4">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the coverage period during which the policy remains active, establishing the timeframe within which the primary beneficiary, Carlos Roberto Martinez, would be entitled to receive the full death benefit if Nicole passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term specified in fact_sentence_1 defines the endpoint required to qualify for the full return-of-premium payment discussed in fact_sentence_2, establishing a direct temporal dependency.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term ensures extended protection, and the lack of war exclusions means the death benefit applies regardless of cause of death, including wartime incidents, enhancing the policy's reliability over its full duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term ensures the policy remains active long enough for aviation-related risks to potentially occur, while the lack of aviation exclusions means those events do not void coverage, making the terms mutually supportive.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe over which the policy operates, during which the absence of hazardous activity exclusions ensures continuous coverage without risk-based limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="b4003548-05a1-4f13-a791-01db074853b9">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe during which the policy remains active, and the absence of travel exclusions ensures that claims related to travel incidents remain eligible throughout this period.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the framework within which the 5-year reinstatement window operates, meaning that even if a lapse occurs early in the term, reinstatement remains possible only up to year 5, limiting the scope of recovery relative to the total term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe during which reinstatement may occur, making it relevant to whether the condition of providing evidence of insurability applies before expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the stage for when reinstatement might occur after a lapse, making it relevant to whether the policyholder can recover coverage under specified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe within which reinstatement may occur, making the survival requirement critical for maintaining coverage continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term enables the return-of-premium feature, justifying why the policy incurs higher costs than standard term life insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses and is subsequently reinstated, the original 20-year term does not govern the ROP calculation—the excluded lapsed period is reset, reducing the total amount refunded even though the nominal term remains 20 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the framework under which reinstatement could occur, triggering a new 2-year suicide and contestability period. Without the long-term commitment defined in the first statement, the reinstatement clause would lack temporal grounding.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
