</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The promise of a fixed $32,400 return depends on consistent, unchanged annual premiums across all 20 years, making the constancy of payments essential to achieving the stated payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 depends on the sustained payment of the $1,620 annual premium over 20 years to trigger the $32,400 return. Without consistent adherence to this recurring payment, the return would not occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The return of $32,400 specified in fact_sentence_1 is contingent upon fulfilling the condition outlined in fact_sentence_2—that all premiums are paid on time. Without punctual payments, the promised refund cannot be received.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The full return of premium described in fact_sentence_1 may be diminished if any premium is paid late, as specified in fact_sentence_2, which imposes a 10% reduction per late payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REDUCTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The return of premium benefit outlined in fact_sentence_1 is conditional upon uninterrupted premium payments; if the policy lapses from non-payment—as stated in fact_sentence_2—the entire refund is lost.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium benefit depends on not exercising the conversion option, as doing so forfeits eligibility for the $32,400 payout. This creates a trade-off between long-term financial returns and access to permanent coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on partial withdrawals reinforces the condition that the $32,400 return is only available upon full compliance and survival to term end, ensuring funds remain intact until maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium benefit described in fact_sentence_1 depends on not exercising the conversion option mentioned in fact_sentence_2, as doing so voids the refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">The absence of policy loans ensures that funds remain intact for the return-of-premium benefit, reinforcing the policy’s design focused solely on guaranteed repayment at maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the outcome of maintaining the policy to term—the $32,400 return—and is supported by fact_sentence_2, which explains that such returns are only available upon full-term survival, reinforcing the conditions under which the refund applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 depends on the policy’s expiration date specified in fact_sentence_2 to determine eligibility for the $32,400 return. Without knowing the end date, it would not be possible to assess whether the condition for repayment was fulfilled.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return specified in fact_sentence_1 corresponds precisely to the total premiums paid over 20 years, confirming it reflects 100% of contributions when the policy is fully maintained.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the general condition under which the return of premium applies; fact_sentence_2 refines it by specifying the required survival date and confirmation of complete premium payments, making the trigger more precise.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 depends on the annual premium stated in fact_sentence_2 to validate the $32,400 return amount, confirming it results from 20 years of consistent payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay the annual premium by September 15 ensures continued policy validity, making it essential for qualifying for the final return of $32,400 after 20 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The promise of a $32,400 return depends entirely on maintaining the policy by paying all required premiums over the 20-year term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the payout condition when the policyholder outlives the term, which complements fact_sentence_2 by defining what happens instead of the death benefit being triggered.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="817d0dcb-1390-42ee-b441-ff53e6769ad8">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return of premium is possible because the policy includes a built-in feature that raises its cost above standard term rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES_INCREASE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="a1786028-dc71-4811-9ab3-5b1cf40851d9">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return-of-premium benefit described in fact_sentence_1 is confirmed to be non-taxable, enhancing its net value to the policyholder.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return of premium is directly enabled by the policy’s higher-than-standard pricing, which funds the guarantee of repayment at maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The full premium refund upon survival applies only if the policy lasts its full duration; however, if death occurs before the term ends, beneficiaries still get a partial refund based on how many years the policy was active, aligning with the same refund schedule used for early surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030">
  <data key="d3">The promise of a $32,400 return of premiums relies on the policy being a pure return-of-premium product without cash value growth, ensuring refunds are limited to actual contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium feature ensures a refund after 20 years if the policyholder outlives the term, which complements the ongoing ability to update beneficiaries without affecting that refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="3a894b15-ff54-4713-9288-259b598b0942">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of a $32,400 return at maturity adds intrinsic value to the policy, making it more attractive as collateral since its future payoff enhances its perceived worth when pledged.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="a176a4ea-8eba-4f29-8ca6-99b1da801960">
  <data key="d3">The first statement specifies the total refund available if the policy lasts its full term, while the second explains that earlier surrender yields a proportional refund based on the ROP schedule, showing flexibility beyond just waiting until maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium feature ensures a refund after 20 years if the policy is kept active, regardless of whether conversion occurs. However, converting to permanent insurance would likely terminate the original term policy’s eligibility for the ROP payout unless specifically allowed under terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the exact amount returned when the policy lasts the full term, which aligns directly with one of the two methods outlined in fact_sentence_2 for accessing cash value: waiting until the end of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 outlines the return-of-premium benefit tied to policy duration, while fact sentence 2 confirms the lack of war exclusion, which affects claim eligibility but not the refund mechanism. These elements address different aspects of policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">The absence of aviation exclusions ensures broader coverage scope, which supports the viability of receiving the return-of-premium benefit regardless of cause of death during the term, assuming survival conditions are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="b4003548-05a1-4f13-a791-01db074853b9">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium provision depends on surviving the entire term without triggering exclusion clauses. Since there are no travel exclusions, the policyholder’s ability to maintain continuous coverage—including fulfilling the conditions for the return—is preserved under normal circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_SUPPORTED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium clause ensures a refund upon surviving the term, unaffected by hazardous activity exclusions, meaning such risks don’t impact the refund eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the policy until maturity ensures a return of premiums, but if the policy lapses, reinstatement becomes necessary, which disrupts eligibility for the original return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The condition that a return of premium is payable only if the policy is maintained until the end of the term implies that lapses would prevent this benefit. This makes reinstatement eligibility under fact_sentence_2 relevant to preserving access to the return.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium clause applies only if the policy remains active throughout the term, making it dependent on avoiding lapses that would trigger reinstatement conditions like paying back premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return of premium is made possible by the policy’s elevated cost, which stems from the return-of-premium feature described in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">The return of premium described in fact_sentence_1 is conditional upon surviving the entire term without lapses. However, if the policy lapses, reinstatement becomes necessary—and this process hinges on the insured being alive, as specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium benefit described in fact_sentence_1 assumes uninterrupted policy maintenance over the entire term, whereas fact_sentence_2 clarifies that reinstating a lapsed policy excludes prior inactive periods from ROP calculations, thereby reducing the eventual refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium benefit depends on surviving the entire term without triggering exclusion clauses like suicide within the initial contestability period. Since reinstatement triggers a new two-year contestability period, any lapse followed by revival could jeopardize eligibility for the return if suicide occurs during that reset window.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
