<edge source="34938dcf-3e35-4563-87da-55be923c02a2" target="005768d3-95ad-47d7-b1be-d0b3a5673f4b">
  <data key="d3">Carlos Roberto Martinez is named as the primary beneficiary, meaning he receives full benefit upon the insured's death unless otherwise specified. Sofia Isabella Martinez, identified as the daughter, is a contingent beneficiary entitled to half the proceeds if the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured or fails to qualify.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ROLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="34938dcf-3e35-4563-87da-55be923c02a2" target="bca9d2c6-7752-46c3-9597-61cc8abf7e89">
  <data key="d3">Carlos Roberto Martinez holds the primary beneficiary position, meaning he receives the death benefit first. Sofia Isabella Martinez serves as a contingent beneficiary, entitled to inherit only if Carlos does not survive the insured or cannot claim the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="34938dcf-3e35-4563-87da-55be923c02a2" target="d51df73f-63ad-42b9-83f4-36facdbba04e">
  <data key="d3">Carlos Roberto Martinez holds the primary beneficiary status, meaning he receives the death benefit first. Marco Daniel Martinez serves as a contingent beneficiary, entitled to the payout only if the primary beneficiary does not survive or cannot claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="34938dcf-3e35-4563-87da-55be923c02a2" target="ce60053c-f1bb-490a-ac19-16ad07280772">
  <data key="d3">Carlos Roberto Martinez holds the primary beneficiary status, meaning he receives the full payout if he outlives the insured. Only if he predeceases or declines the benefit would the contingent share be activated, splitting equally between Sofia and Marco.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINGENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
