  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="005768d3-95ad-47d7-b1be-d0b3a5673f4b">
  <data key="d3">The policy has a 20-year term duration, which defines its coverage period. This detail is separate from the identification of Sofia Isabella Martinez as a beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="ac78d07a-693a-4a41-896b-89ccec21e2ab">
  <data key="d3">The policy has a fixed 20-year term, determining when coverage ends and whether the full premiums are refunded upon survival. This timeframe does not affect the identification of Marco Daniel Martinez as a contingent beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="bca9d2c6-7752-46c3-9597-61cc8abf7e89">
  <data key="d3">The policy has a fixed 20-year term, defining the period during which the death benefit is active. This duration does not affect Sofia Isabella Martinez’s status as a contingent beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="d51df73f-63ad-42b9-83f4-36facdbba04e">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term duration determines the period during which the policy provides coverage and eligibility for premium refund. It does not affect who qualifies as a beneficiary like Marco Daniel Martinez.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="ce60053c-f1bb-490a-ac19-16ad07280772">
  <data key="d3">The policy's 20-year term defines its active period but has no bearing on how benefits are distributed among contingent beneficiaries upon a claim event.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term duration directly applies to the described Return of Premium (ROP) Term Life Insurance Policy, specifying how long coverage remains active under the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the condition under which the premium refund becomes applicable; without fulfilling this duration, the return does not occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="0ff7a95c-a146-4ec1-9ada-e9ee6ce46b31">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term duration defines the coverage period but does not influence or relate directly to the availability of converting to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="5ff7a5d2-f300-426c-a845-7a6982ac1054">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe during which the policy offers life insurance protection. Without specifying the duration, the nature and applicability of the protection would lack context.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe under which the policy's return-of-premium feature applies. If the insured survives this period and has fulfilled premium obligations, the full amount is refunded.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the timeframe over which the $32,400 in premiums were paid, establishing the duration for which coverage and potential refund eligibility apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">OVERLAPS_IN_TIME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the window during which the insured's death triggers the payout. Without this specified duration, it would not be clear when the death benefit applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="56d974f0-7976-40f7-a400-a08ec69d94ac">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the coverage window, during which the $300,000 death benefit becomes payable if the insured dies. This ensures the benefit is available only within the specified timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES DURING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="e8f2bfea-e66b-488f-86a1-43ceaf048efd">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the window during which the death benefit applies; if the insured dies within this period, they qualify for the death benefit along with a prorated portion of the returned premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the window during which coverage applies; however, submitting a government-issued ID is required only after a claim is made, regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="834d28a5-622d-4fec-8a75-c824a028663b">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the window during which a death benefit may be claimed; thus, the need for a certified death certificate arises only if the insured dies within that period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe during which claims may arise, making it relevant background for understanding when the claim submission requirement applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term ensures the death benefit of $300,000 remains applicable if the insured passes away within this timeframe, making the benefit conditional upon the policy's duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term duration enables the calculation of proportional premium refunds upon early death, linking the policy's lifespan to payout conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the period over which the $1,620 annual premium is paid, ensuring the policy’s return-of-premium feature is available upon survival.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term enables predictable, stable premium payments, ensuring the policy's return-of-premium feature can be fulfilled if all conditions are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe within which annual premiums must be paid consistently to fulfill conditions for returning all premiums. Without timely payments on September 15 each year, the return benefit may be forfeited.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe within which consistent premium payments are required to secure the return of premiums; failure to maintain payments leads to forfeiture of this benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term enables the return of premiums, but only if all premiums are paid on schedule, making the timing and consistency of payments essential to fulfilling the benefit outlined in the initial statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term enables eligibility for the return of premiums, but this benefit is conditional upon timely payments; any late payment reduces it by 10%, undermining the full payout promised under the original terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term ensures long-term coverage, and the absence of war exclusions means the policy remains active even if death occurs due to wartime events during this period.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term duration ensures eligibility for full ROP payout upon policy expiration, making it essential for accessing cash value under the "wait until end" option detailed in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the timeframe during which the death benefit applies, except in cases like suicide within the initial two years, which nullifies that benefit regardless of timing within the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO_TERM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the overall lifespan of the policy, under which the two-year contestability window operates. This means any challenge to the policy's validity due to misrepresentation would occur within the earliest phase of the 20-year coverage period.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term ensures the policy's longevity, making the absence of aviation exclusions meaningful throughout the entire coverage period. This enhances overall protection under the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term aligns with the policy’s lack of hazardous activity exclusions, ensuring continuous coverage over the full term regardless of high-risk pursuits. This consistency supports broader protection scope across the policy's lifespan.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the maximum lifespan of the policy, making it relevant to determining eligibility for reinstatement under the five-year rule mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the foundational period for the policy’s operation, under which the possibility of reinstatement within five years after a lapse becomes relevant. This ensures that even if coverage ends early due to non-payment, the policyholder retains limited options to restore protection before expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term sets the maximum lifespan of the policy, influencing whether reinstatement under clause 2 remains viable before expiration. Without surviving past the term, reinstatement becomes irrelevant.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the maximum lifespan of the policy, underpinning when reinstatement may be considered viable—if the insured remains alive after a lapse. Survival past lapses is essential for reinstating coverage within the original term’s boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term duration allows for the return of premiums upon policy expiration, which explains why this policy has a higher cost compared to standard term policies without such a benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the core duration of the policy, but reinstatement after a lapse activates a new 2-year suicide and contestability period, introducing conditional limitations on benefit eligibility even within the original term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term defines the original coverage window, and upon reinstatement, the ROP benefit is recalculated excluding any lapsed period, meaning the effective term used for calculating refunds depends on the remaining active portion of the original 20-year span.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
