<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="55fb2d1d-cd7c-45a8-ac06-1cf18f6fa769">
  <data key="d3">The policy guarantees full refund of premiums if the insured lives through the 20-year term. This feature applies regardless of beneficiary designation, including when Carlos Roberto Martinez is the designated primary beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_OUTCOME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="34938dcf-3e35-4563-87da-55be923c02a2">
  <data key="d3">The policy returns 100% of premiums if the insured lives through the 20-year term, regardless of beneficiary details. This condition stands independently from who receives the payout upon death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="2092accb-1370-4d13-a1f1-a49167717503">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s provision to return 100% of premiums upon surviving the term applies specifically to the policy owner, who is confirmed as Carlos Roberto Martinez.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENTITLED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="005768d3-95ad-47d7-b1be-d0b3a5673f4b">
  <data key="d3">The policy returns 100% of premiums if the insured survives the 20-year term. This outcome is independent of the identity or share of any beneficiary, including Sofia Isabella Martinez.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="ac78d07a-693a-4a41-896b-89ccec21e2ab">
  <data key="d3">The policy returns 100% of premiums if the insured survives the 20-year term, regardless of beneficiary designations like Marco Daniel Martinez’s status as son. His identity is unrelated to the refund mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="bca9d2c6-7752-46c3-9597-61cc8abf7e89">
  <data key="d3">The policy returns 100% of premiums if the insured survives the 20-year term, regardless of beneficiary designations. This condition applies independently of who receives benefits upon death, including Sofia Isabella Martinez as a contingent beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="d51df73f-63ad-42b9-83f4-36facdbba04e">
  <data key="d3">The policy returns 100% of premiums if the insured survives the 20-year term, ensuring financial recovery for the policyholder. This scenario is unrelated to beneficiary designations like Marco Daniel Martinez’s role as a contingent recipient, which applies exclusively when the insured dies before the term ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="ce60053c-f1bb-490a-ac19-16ad07280772">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that full premium repayment occurs only if the insured lives through the entire 20-year term. This outcome has no bearing on how the death benefit is distributed among beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">The promise to return 100% of premiums upon surviving the term defines a core characteristic of a Return of Premium (ROP) term life insurance policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">Surviving the 20-year term triggers the return of all premiums, meaning the length of the term determines eligibility for this financial benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">If the insured survives the 20-year term, they receive a refund equal to all premiums paid—specifically $32,400—as stated in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="0ff7a95c-a146-4ec1-9ada-e9ee6ce46b31">
  <data key="d3">The policy returning all premiums upon surviving the term does not affect or influence the availability of converting to permanent insurance later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the general principle that all premiums are refunded if the insured survives the term. Fact_sentence_2 specifies the exact refund amount of $32,400 when this occurs, illustrating the application of the general rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="5ff7a5d2-f300-426c-a845-7a6982ac1054">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums upon survival relies on the policy's original intent to provide life insurance protection throughout the term. Without this protective function, the condition for premium refund would lack significance.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes what happens if the insured lives through the term—premiums are refunded. This outcome contrasts directly with fact_sentence_2, which applies only if the insured dies before the term ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="56d974f0-7976-40f7-a400-a08ec69d94ac">
  <data key="d3">The first fact outlines what happens if the insured lives through the term, resulting in a refund of premiums. This does not affect the second fact, which specifies the fixed death benefit payable only if the insured dies before the end of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="e8f2bfea-e66b-488f-86a1-43ceaf048efd">
  <data key="d3">When the insured survives the term, full premiums are refunded. This refund occurs independently of whether a death benefit is claimed; it applies only when the insured outlives the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="834d28a5-622d-4fec-8a75-c824a028663b">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns premium repayment if the insured outlives the policy term, whereas the second specifies documentation needed for a death benefit claim. They pertain to distinct claims processes based on different outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09">
  <data key="d3">The first statement explains what happens if the insured outlives the term, focusing on premium refund eligibility. The second statement details documentation required when making a claim after death, but it does not relate directly to survival outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums upon surviving the term has no bearing on the documentation required for a claim after death. This statement concerns post-term financial settlement, while the second addresses claim submission procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of premium return upon surviving the term complements the policyowner’s ability to modify beneficiaries, reinforcing overall control over the policy's outcome and distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9">
  <data key="d3">The promise of returning 100% of premiums upon survival necessitates higher initial payments, which justifies the increased cost relative to standard term policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_REASON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="817d0dcb-1390-42ee-b441-ff53e6769ad8">
  <data key="d3">The promise of returning 100% of premiums upon survival directly justifies the increased cost of the policy compared to standard term life insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES_INCREASE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">If the insured survives the 20-year term, the entire premium sum is returned; otherwise, if death occurs during the term, beneficiaries receive the full death benefit along with a prorated refund based on time elapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The first fact outlines full premium repayment if the insured survives the term; the second extends this logic by specifying that partial refunds apply if death occurs earlier, aligning with the same refund schedule used for early surrenders.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that all premiums be paid on time to receive a full refund depends on meeting the annual due date specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of level premiums supports the feasibility of returning 100% of paid premiums, ensuring policyholders can reliably meet payment requirements to qualify for the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums described in fact_sentence_1 depends directly on meeting the payment obligation outlined in fact_sentence_2. Without on-time premium payments, the full refund cannot be received.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 depends on the consistent payment of the annual premium specified in fact_sentence_2 to trigger the full refund of premiums upon surviving the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums described in fact_sentence_1 depends on continuous premium payments; if those payments are not maintained, as stated in fact_sentence_2, the benefit is lost entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The return of 100% of premiums upon surviving the term depends on timely payments; late payments during the grace period reduce this refund by 10%, undermining the full benefit outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that 100% of premiums are returned if the insured survives the 20-year term, which corresponds exactly to the final condition mentioned in fact_sentence_2 about receiving full ROP payment at term’s end.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums clause applies only if the insured survives the entire term, which excludes cases where death occurs from suicide within the first two years. This condition ensures that the insurer does not pay out returns when the risk was intentionally triggered shortly after coverage began.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIES_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums at the end of the term is contingent on the validity of the policy, which can be challenged if material misrepresentations were made in the initial application within the first two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">The absence of hazardous activity exclusions means the policy remains intact even if the insured engages in risky behavior, ensuring eligibility for the full premium return if they survive the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums upon surviving the term is unaffected by the lack of aviation exclusions, which ensures payouts remain intact regardless of cause of death, including aviation-related events.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the insured remain alive enables reinstatement after a lapse, preserving the possibility of qualifying for the full return of premiums at the end of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">The first fact outlines a benefit tied to timely premium payments over the entire term, while the second explains consequences and requirements if those payments fail. Together, they frame the importance of consistent premium payment across the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The first fact outlines premium refund eligibility at term end, whereas the second explains requirements to revive a lapsed policy. They address different lifecycle stages of the same policy but do not directly influence each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums upon surviving the term depends on continuous coverage without disqualifying events; the lack of war exclusions ensures such an event doesn't void the policy’s terms, thereby indirectly supporting eligibility for the premium refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums depends on continuous coverage over the full 20-year term; lapses may prevent eligibility unless successfully reinstated, though reinstatement does not guarantee retention of prior ROP accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums depends on continuous coverage over the full term; if the policy lapses and is reinstated, the accumulated ROP benefit is reset, reducing the total amount potentially recoverable.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The promise of returning 100% of premiums upon survival (fact_sentence_1) is enabled by the increased cost of the policy, which stems from the added ROP feature described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums depends on surviving the initial 20-year term without lapses; however, reinstating the policy triggers a new contestability period, potentially affecting whether claims—including those tied to long-term survival—are honored.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
