  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The total premium sum of $32,400 reflects the cumulative cost over 20 years, but its full refund depends on uninterrupted, on-time payments as mandated by the policy’s conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The total premium amount of $32,400 depends on paying $1,620 annually on September 15 each year for 20 years. Missing any deadline risks losing the full refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The total premium amount stated in fact_sentence_1 depends on timely payments; any delay would reduce the returnable sum by 10%, undermining the expectation of full repayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return of premiums described in fact_sentence_1 is contingent upon consistent premium payments, which would be jeopardized if any payment were missed—as specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid ($32,400) represent the full amount eligible for return under the ROP provision, which is accessible only at term end or via surrender per specified rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid ($32,400) determine the refundable amount at policy maturity, but this refund is conditional on surviving beyond the term without triggering exclusions like suicide within two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f">
  <data key="d3">The total premium payment of $32,400 depends on the policy remaining uncontested; if material misrepresentation is found within two years, the insurer may deny the return of premiums despite full payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid ($32,400) are relevant because they determine the refundable amount at the end of the term, while the lack of hazardous activity exclusions ensures broader coverage scope, reinforcing the policy’s comprehensive nature despite its higher cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid reflect the financial commitment tied to the policy’s return-of-premium guarantee, while the lack of war exclusions ensures broader eligibility for claims under normal circumstances, supporting the policy's comprehensive risk coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid ($32,400) determine the refundable amount at the end of the term, while the absence of aviation exclusions ensures broader eligibility for claims, including those involving air travel accidents.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, the ability to reinstate it ensures continuity of coverage and preserves the right to receive the full premium refund at the end of the term, assuming future premiums are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid reflect the financial commitment required to qualify for a full return at the end of the term, whereas reinstating a lapsed policy depends on proving insurability, which may affect future eligibility for such returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid ($32,400) determine the maximum return upon surviving the term, but reinstating the policy requires the insured’s survival—an ongoing prerequisite for accessing those funds should the policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid reflect the upfront financial commitment required to maintain coverage over 20 years, whereas reinstatement requires repaying missed premiums with interest—indicating that failure to meet these commitments could lead to lapsation and subsequent costs to restore coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid ($32,400) serve as the baseline for the ROP benefit, but if the policy lapses and is later reinstated, the returnable amount is recalculated excluding the lapsed period, thereby affecting the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The high total premium payment reflects the added cost associated with the return-of-premium benefit, which ensures full reimbursement at the end of the term if no claims occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The total premiums paid ($32,400) are only fully recoverable if the policyholder survives the original term without triggering exclusion clauses like suicide within the initial contestability period. However, reinstatement triggers a new two-year contestability period, meaning any suicide attempt during this renewed window could void the return of premiums even if the original term was fulfilled.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
