  <data key="d3">The refund of $32,400 depends on surviving the entire 20-year term, making the term length a prerequisite for triggering the payout described in sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 gives a concrete example by stating that $32,400 is returned upon surviving the term. This supports and concretizes the broader statement in fact_sentence_1 about returning 100% of premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder survives the 20-year term and has made full payments, they receive back exactly the total amount paid—$32,400—in full.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="5ff7a5d2-f300-426c-a845-7a6982ac1054">
  <data key="d3">The policy's return of premiums upon surviving the term complements its function as a protective life insurance product over the specified period.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="0ff7a95c-a146-4ec1-9ada-e9ee6ce46b31">
  <data key="d3">The policy's return of premium at maturity does not affect its ability to allow conversion to permanent insurance later. This benefit is independent of any future underwriting flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="e8f2bfea-e66b-488f-86a1-43ceaf048efd">
  <data key="d3">If the insured survives the term, the full premium amount is refunded. This refund occurs independently of the death benefit, which applies only if the insured dies during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="834d28a5-622d-4fec-8a75-c824a028663b">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s premium refund upon surviving the term does not influence or relate to the documentation required for a death benefit claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="56d974f0-7976-40f7-a400-a08ec69d94ac">
  <data key="d3">If the insured survives the 20-year term and pays all premiums, the policy refunds $32,400. This outcome contrasts with the scenario where the insured dies, triggering a $300,000 death benefit instead.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f">
  <data key="d3">The policy returning funds upon surviving the term does not influence or relate to the identification documents required by beneficiaries when claiming benefits post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d">
  <data key="d3">If the insured survives the 20-year term and has paid all premiums, the policy refunds the total premiums. This outcome contrasts with the scenario where the insured dies during the term, triggering a $300,000 benefit payment to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains the financial outcome if the insured lives through the term, while fact_sentence_2 details documentation required when a claim is filed after death. These pertain to separate events and outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return upon survival is enabled by the policy’s higher-than-standard pricing, reflecting its guarantee of premium reimbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438">
  <data key="d3">The survival-based premium return described in fact_sentence_1 is unaffected by changes to beneficiaries, which are governed by separate policy provisions outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="817d0dcb-1390-42ee-b441-ff53e6769ad8">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return of premiums upon survival is the reason why this policy costs more than standard term life insurance, creating a direct cause-effect relationship between the benefit and the higher premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES_INCREASE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">If the insured survives the 20-year term and all premiums are paid, the policy returns $32,400; otherwise, if death occurs within the term, beneficiaries receive the $300,000 death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_OUTCOME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the full premium return upon survival after 20 years; fact_sentence_2 extends this logic by specifying that similar refund rules apply pro rata if death occurs earlier, ensuring consistency across outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The condition for returning $32,400 hinges on consistent annual payments, including those due on September 15, ensuring compliance with the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the financial outcome of surviving the term under ideal conditions, while fact_sentence_2 clarifies that timely premium payments are required to achieve that outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed return of $32,400 depends on consistent, level premium payments over 20 years, which ensures no increases disrupt the ability to meet eligibility requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return upon surviving the 20-year term corresponds precisely to 20 annual premiums of $1,620, validating the expected payout under consistent payment conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The return of $32,400 depends on no late premium payments; if a premium is paid late, the amount received is reduced by 10%, undermining the full payout described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The return of premium benefit depends on timely payment of all premiums; failure to do so leads to forfeiture of the payout mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f">
  <data key="d3">If the insured survived the term but misrepresented information at application, the insurer could void the premium return despite meeting survival conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the exact return amount ($32,400) under the condition of survival and timely payments, which corresponds to the final ROP payout mentioned in fact_sentence_2 when the term ends without lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s return of premiums upon survival depends on meeting all contractual obligations, including avoiding exclusions like suicide or fraud. The absence of war exclusions ensures that such events do not void the return benefit, supporting overall policy integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202">
  <data key="d3">The first fact outlines a financial return when the insured survives the term, whereas the second specifies an exception to death benefit eligibility due to suicide early in the policy term. These clauses address different scenarios—one about survival and refund, the other about premature death under specific circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">The absence of hazardous activity exclusions ensures wider eligibility under the policy, which indirectly supports the conditions under which the return of premiums could apply, though it doesn't alter the mechanics of the payout itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPRTS_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">The policy's return of premium clause ensures financial recovery if the insured survives the term, which is unaffected by the lack of aviation exclusions. The absence of such exclusions enhances overall coverage integrity, ensuring broader eligibility for claims including those involving aviation-related deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, the condition required to receive the $32,400 return may be jeopardized unless reinstated within five years, making timely reinstatement critical to preserving the original benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The first fact outlines the financial return available upon successful completion of the policy term, while the second explains what is required to restore coverage after it has lapsed. Together, they address different stages of policy lifecycle management—survival outcome versus restoration after failure to maintain payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a reward for uninterrupted premium payments over 20 years, whereas fact_sentence_2 explains consequences and requirements when such payments fail. Both involve premium-related outcomes but apply to different scenarios—one for success, the other for remediation after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses and is later reinstated, the return-of-premium benefit is adjusted to exclude the inactive period, reducing the total refund compared to what would be received under uninterrupted coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, it may be reinstated only if the insured is still alive, which affects whether the eventual return of premium becomes available. This condition ensures continuity of eligibility for the $32,400 payout at term end.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return upon survival is enabled by the return-of-premium feature, which inherently increases the policy's overall cost compared to standard term life insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses and is subsequently reinstated, the original terms for returning premiums may be affected because a new two-year contestability period begins, potentially invalidating claims including the return of premiums if suicide occurs during this phase.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
