<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="55fb2d1d-cd7c-45a8-ac06-1cf18f6fa769">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 death benefit is payable only if the insured dies during the term; since Carlos Roberto Martinez is the designated primary beneficiary, he is the intended recipient of that amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">PAYABLE TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="34938dcf-3e35-4563-87da-55be923c02a2">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 death benefit is payable only if the insured dies during the policy term, ensuring that Carlos Roberto Martinez, as the primary beneficiary, receives the funds under those conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON DEATH DURING TERM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="2092accb-1370-4d13-a1f1-a49167717503">
  <data key="d3">The policy pays $300,000 to the beneficiary if the insured dies during the term, though this outcome does not depend on who owns the policy, such as Carlos Roberto Martinez.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="005768d3-95ad-47d7-b1be-d0b3a5673f4b">
  <data key="d3">The policy pays $300,000 to the designated beneficiary(ies) if the insured dies during the term, including scenarios where Sofia Isabella Martinez inherits due to her status as a contingent beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_BENEFICIARY_STATUS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="ac78d07a-693a-4a41-896b-89ccec21e2ab">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 death benefit is payable only if the insured dies during the term; since Marco Daniel Martinez is listed as a contingent beneficiary, he qualifies to receive half of that amount under such circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">QUALIFIES BENEFICIARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="bca9d2c6-7752-46c3-9597-61cc8abf7e89">
  <data key="d3">The payment of $300,000 upon the insured's death during the term enables the distribution of funds to contingent beneficiaries like Sofia Isabella Martinez, who are specified under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGER_FOR_BENEFICIARY_PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="d51df73f-63ad-42b9-83f4-36facdbba04e">
  <data key="d3">The payout of $300,000 occurs when the insured dies during the term, enabling contingent beneficiaries like Marco Daniel Martinez to receive funds based on the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="ce60053c-f1bb-490a-ac19-16ad07280772">
  <data key="d3">The payment of $300,000 upon the insured’s death during the term depends on the designated beneficiary structure, including the 50/50 split between Sofia and Marco.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence specifies the death benefit amount payable when the insured dies during the term, which only applies within the scope of the ROP term policy introduced in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">The potential payment of $300,000 upon death only occurs within the defined 20-year period; thus, the outcome relies on the existence of that timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains the payout condition when the insured dies during the term, which negates the possibility of premium refund under fact_sentence_1 since the event triggers immediate benefit distribution rather than maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">The promise of a $300,000 death benefit incentivizes the policyholder to pay the full $32,400 in premiums over the 20 years to maintain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCENTIVIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the policy term while it remains active, the beneficiary receives $300,000. This event precludes the possibility of premium repayment, which only occurs if the insured lives through the entire term.</data>
  <data key="d4">MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="5ff7a5d2-f300-426c-a845-7a6982ac1054">
  <data key="d3">The promise of a $300,000 death benefit serves as the key protective feature underpinning the policy’s life insurance function during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="0ff7a95c-a146-4ec1-9ada-e9ee6ce46b31">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit provision ensures financial protection upon passing during the term; however, it operates independently of whether the policyholder chooses to convert to permanent coverage later.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="834d28a5-622d-4fec-8a75-c824a028663b">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit payout depends on submitting proper documentation, including a certified death certificate, which ensures claims are verified before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 requires submission of a claim form as part of the claims process. Without completing this step, the benefit cannot be accessed.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="56d974f0-7976-40f7-a400-a08ec69d94ac">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the conditions under which the death benefit is triggered; fact_sentence_2 clarifies the exact amount of that benefit. Together, they define the core financial outcome tied to the policy’s purpose.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="e8f2bfea-e66b-488f-86a1-43ceaf048efd">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies during the term, the $300,000 death benefit is paid out, and this payment happens concurrently with a partial refund of premiums based on how much was paid up to that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">ADDITIONAL_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit payment depends on submitting proper documentation, including a government-issued ID, to validate the claim after the insured’s passing during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit of $300,000 includes an additional proportional refund of premiums based on how long the policy was active before the insured’s death, enhancing the total payout to beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that the $300,000 death benefit is paid upon the insured's death during the term, which is confirmed and reiterated by fact_sentence_2 stating beneficiaries receive the full amount under the same condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
