</edge>
<edge source="834d28a5-622d-4fec-8a75-c824a028663b" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate applies only when a claim is made due to the insured's passing, which contrasts with the scenario described in the first sentence where the insured survives. There is no direct influence between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="834d28a5-622d-4fec-8a75-c824a028663b" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is a mandatory step in initiating a claim, ensuring legitimacy before any benefit disbursement occurs. While unrelated directly to the amount of premiums paid, it underscores procedural requirements tied to the policy's outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="834d28a5-622d-4fec-8a75-c824a028663b" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is necessary for claims but has no bearing on whether premiums are refunded at the end of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
