  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a completed claim form applies specifically to beneficiaries like Carlos Roberto Martinez, whose status as the primary beneficiary makes him responsible for initiating the claim procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="34938dcf-3e35-4563-87da-55be923c02a2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a completed claim form applies specifically to beneficiaries like Carlos Roberto Martinez, ensuring only authorized individuals can access the policy proceeds.</data>
  <data key="d4">MANDATES_SUBMISSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="2092accb-1370-4d13-a1f1-a49167717503">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is a necessary procedural step for beneficiaries to receive benefits. Since Carlos Roberto Martinez holds sole ownership, he has the capacity to initiate or support this process on behalf of the beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="005768d3-95ad-47d7-b1be-d0b3a5673f4b">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiaries, including Sofia Isabella Martinez, must submit a completed claim form to initiate a payout. Her eligibility stems from her designation as a contingent beneficiary under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="ac78d07a-693a-4a41-896b-89ccec21e2ab">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for beneficiaries to submit a completed claim form applies specifically to individuals such as Marco Daniel Martinez, who is named as a contingent beneficiary under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="bca9d2c6-7752-46c3-9597-61cc8abf7e89">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a completed claim form applies specifically to beneficiaries like Sofia Isabella Martinez, who may inherit under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="d51df73f-63ad-42b9-83f4-36facdbba04e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a completed claim form applies specifically to beneficiaries like Marco Daniel Martinez who may be entitled to benefits upon the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="ce60053c-f1bb-490a-ac19-16ad07280772">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is a mandatory step before any benefit payout, regardless of how the contingent beneficiaries are designated. It ensures proper verification prior to disbursement based on the stated beneficiary arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is a required action that arises directly from the existence of a Return of Premium (ROP) Term Life Insurance Policy, ensuring proper benefit distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a claim form is necessary whenever a death benefit is sought, particularly within the 20-year window defined by the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMEFRAME_DEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">The second statement specifies that a claim form is needed when filing a death benefit claim. This process is unrelated to whether the insured survived the term or received a premium refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a claim form is required to access benefits, independent of how much was paid in premiums. While premiums determine eligibility for refund upon survival, the claim form is necessary regardless of payout type.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 requires submission of a claim form for death benefit claims, whereas fact_sentence_1 applies only if the insured survives the entire term without any claim being made. The two sentences describe unrelated situations.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="5ff7a5d2-f300-426c-a845-7a6982ac1054">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is part of the procedure that enables beneficiaries to access the death benefit promised under the policy’s life insurance protection during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="0ff7a95c-a146-4ec1-9ada-e9ee6ce46b31">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is required for benefit distribution; however, this step is independent of whether the policyholder chooses to convert to permanent coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a claim form enables the processing of the death benefit outlined in fact_sentence_1, making it essential for accessing the promised payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="56d974f0-7976-40f7-a400-a08ec69d94ac">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is necessary to trigger the release of the death benefit, which is set at $300,000. While the form initiates the process, its content does not alter the fixed benefit amount specified in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR_PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="834d28a5-622d-4fec-8a75-c824a028663b">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form follows the submission of a certified death certificate, serving as the formal request for benefit disbursement after eligibility has been confirmed through the death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="e8f2bfea-e66b-488f-86a1-43ceaf048efd">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is required to initiate the process that leads to the disbursement of the death benefit and potential premium refunds, making it essential for accessing the coverage's full value.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that a completed claim form is mandatory for claims. This requirement complements fact sentence 2, which specifies that a government-issued ID is also needed, together forming essential parts of the document package for processing a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">While the claim submission requirement ensures proper processing of death benefits, it has no bearing on whether a return of premium is received at the end of the term due to survival.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">Knowing that a claim form is required helps contextualize the importance of timely documentation after the insured's passing, especially since the $300,000 death benefit depends on proper submission—this ties back to the financial details like the $1,620 annual premium that sustain coverage eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
