<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="d51df73f-63ad-42b9-83f4-36facdbba04e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a government-issued ID applies to all beneficiaries, including contingent ones like Marco Daniel Martinez, ensuring proper verification before payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="ce60053c-f1bb-490a-ac19-16ad07280772">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID as part of a claim is an administrative step unrelated to how benefits are distributed among contingent beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID is part of the procedural requirements for claiming benefits under any term life insurance policy, including one with a Return of Premium feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">Providing a government-issued ID is part of the claim process that occurs post-death, independent of the policy’s fixed 20-year term length.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID is necessary only when making a claim after death, unrelated to whether premiums are refunded due to survival. It pertains solely to the claims process, not premium repayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiaries must submit a government-issued ID to file a claim, regardless of how much was paid in premiums. The submission of identification is independent of the total premium amount paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID during a claim process is unrelated to whether the policy pays out money at the end of the term due to survival.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="5ff7a5d2-f300-426c-a845-7a6982ac1054">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID is required when claiming benefits, which only become applicable if the insured dies during the policy’s term, as outlined in the initial protective function of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="0ff7a95c-a146-4ec1-9ada-e9ee6ce46b31">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID during a claim is part of the verification procedure unrelated to whether the policyholder may convert the term coverage into permanent insurance later.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID is a prerequisite step needed to initiate and complete the process of receiving the death benefit under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="56d974f0-7976-40f7-a400-a08ec69d94ac">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID is necessary to verify identity when claiming the $300,000 death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="834d28a5-622d-4fec-8a75-c824a028663b">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID verifies the beneficiary’s identity, whereas a certified death certificate proves the insured has died. These steps work side-by-side in validating eligibility without one depending on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="e8f2bfea-e66b-488f-86a1-43ceaf048efd">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a government-issued ID is required to initiate a claim, which may lead to receipt of the death benefit and potential premium refund described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="26e92023-05f0-4e85-a993-49935b7f2e09">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 requires a government-issued ID from beneficiaries, which supports the process described in fact sentence 1 about submitting a claim form, ensuring identity verification alongside formal claim initiation.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">The second fact details procedural steps for claiming benefits after death, which contrasts with the first fact about returning premiums only if the policyholder lives through the entire term. One applies to survival, the other to death-related claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80b3a0f3-2ae7-4269-ae27-bcba28448f8f" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">Providing a government ID is part of the claim procedure that enables beneficiaries to collect the $300,000 death benefit, which is funded through consistent payments like the $1,620 annual premium specified in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
