<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">Receiving $32,400 requires being alive on September 15, 2044—the precise endpoint of the policy term. Thus, the payout hinges entirely on reaching this terminus.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 payout upon survival at maturity corresponds exactly to the total premiums paid over the 20-year term, representing a full refund of contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">The full return of premiums at maturity (year 20) aligns with the surrender refund scale, where year 20 yields 100%. This illustrates how the matured outcome fits into the broader early surrender framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">The full premium return described in fact_sentence_1 only applies after sustained compliance over 20 years; fact_sentence_2 explains that such returns are unavailable during the initial five years, establishing temporal boundaries for eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">The survival-based ROP payout at maturity is unrelated to the early surrender refund rate during mid-term years. One applies only if the insured lives through the full term, while the other applies only if the policy is terminated earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 details the financial return when the insured survives the entire term, whereas fact_sentence_2 explains what happens if the insured passes away earlier. These are parallel provisions covering distinct events.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE OUTCOME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">The first statement outlines the full refund available only after surviving the entire 20-year period. The second details a partial refund rate that applies during mid-term surrenders, specifically years 11–15, reflecting a graduated refund scale over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the maximum refund available after 20 years of survival, which aligns with the end point of the refund scale referenced in fact_sentence_2. The 90% refund in Years 16–19 serves as a step toward reaching the 100% refund specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 details the full refund condition if the insured survives to the end of the term, while fact sentence 2 explains that the same refund calculation applies when the insured dies before the term ends, ensuring consistency in payout rules regardless of outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">The payout described in fact_sentence_1 occurs when the policy reaches its final year (Year 20), where the return-of-premium feature triggers a 100% refund. This matches the surrender provision stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">The policyholder receives $32,400 upon surviving to September 15, 2044, if all premiums were paid; this payment is issued within 60 days of that event date.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_WITHIN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return relies on paying $1,620 per year for 20 years; without this consistent payment schedule, the lump-sum refund would not occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">For the policyholder to qualify for the $32,400 return, they must have fulfilled all premium obligations. The annual premium due on September 15 ensures ongoing compliance with this requirement across the policy’s duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The full return of premium depends on having paid all premiums over the policy term. Without fulfilling this requirement, the payout specified in the first sentence does not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that premiums remain unchanged ensures consistent payments, enabling the accumulation of the full $32,400 needed for the Return of Premium upon survival to the policy's maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains the financial outcome tied to reaching the date stated in fact_sentence_1, confirming that the $32,400 refund is due only if the insured survives to September 15, 2044, and all premiums are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the conditions under which the $32,400 refund is triggered, confirming that it results from paying $1,620 per year over 20 years, thus validating the figure stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the specific deadline (September 15, 2044) and conditions (full premium payments) needed for the return; fact_sentence_1 confirms that meeting these criteria results in a $32,400 payout, validating the outcome described in sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 refund specified in fact_sentence_1 is enabled by the higher premium pricing mentioned in fact_sentence_2, reflecting the added cost of the return-of-premium feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="817d0dcb-1390-42ee-b441-ff53e6769ad8">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return of premium is enabled by the policy’s design, which justifies its increased cost relative to standard term insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_REASON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">The condition for receiving the $32,400 ROP is unaffected by any prior misstatement of the insured's age, ensuring consistent payout eligibility despite potential underwriting errors.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314" target="a176a4ea-8eba-4f29-8ca6-99b1da801960">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the specific outcome of surviving to the maturity date with full premium payments, while fact_sentence_2 explains the broader right to access returns via surrender, including the possibility of receiving part of those funds earlier under the ROP schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
