<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">The amount $32,400 being equal to 100% of premiums paid confirms that it corresponds exactly to the cumulative payments made by the policyholder over the entire 20-year term, culminating on September 15, 2044.</data>
  <data key="d4">FULFILLS_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 received at maturity is justified because it matches 100% of the cumulative premiums paid throughout the policy’s duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 figure serves as the maximum refundable amount under the ROP clause, achieved only if the policy is held to maturity. This benchmark informs the variable refund rates applied when surrender occurs earlier than year 20.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">The total accumulated premiums of $32,400 serve as the basis for calculating partial refunds under the early surrender provisions. During Years 6–10, 30% of this sum is returned if the policy is surrendered.</data>
  <data key="d4">BASES_REFUND</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 refund corresponds to full premium payments over 20 years, but this payout is contingent on surviving the entire term; otherwise, refunds are reduced based on duration, including none in the initial five years.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">The total premium sum of $32,400 serves as the basis for calculating partial refunds; thus, 60% of this amount corresponds to the refund available during Years 11–15 under early surrender conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">BASES_REFUND</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 figure corresponds exactly to the full refund available after 20 years if the policy is surrendered, validating the cumulative payment sum described in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 refund corresponds to 100% of accumulated premiums after 20 years, while the 90% refund rate in Years 16–19 reflects a progressive reduction from the maximum return, showing the scaling mechanism before full repayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 refund amount corresponds to full premium repayment under the ROP clause when conditions are met. This sum triggers a payout obligation fulfilled within 60 days of the qualifying event.</data>
  <data key="d4">PAYMENT_TIMING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The total premium sum of $32,400 serves as the baseline for computing proportional refunds under the early surrender schedule when a claim arises due to death during the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">BASES REFUND</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains the total accumulated premiums eligible for return if the policyholder outlives the term. This information does not influence or depend on the payout details described in fact_sentence_2 regarding death benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">The total sum of $32,400 in premiums paid over 20 years is derived directly from the annual payment of $1,620 multiplied by the number of years.</data>
  <data key="d4">CALCULATES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The full return of $32,400 depends entirely on fulfilling the requirement of paying all premiums throughout the 20-year term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The claim that $32,400 is 100% of premiums paid relies on the assumption that payments remain constant; without stable, unchanging premiums, this total would not hold true.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 relies on the knowledge of the annual premium and policy length to calculate the total payments. Fact_sentence_2 establishes the consistent annual payment schedule required to reach that cumulative total.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">The statement that $32,400 equals 100% of premiums paid implies it is returned only after completing the entire 20-year term, which concludes precisely on September 15, 2044, as specified in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 returned upon survival reflects exactly 20 years of $1,620 annual premiums, confirming the figure cited in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that $32,400 is equivalent to 100% of premiums paid, directly supporting the claim in fact_sentence_1 about the refund amount upon surviving the full term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 in premiums reflects the financial commitment required by the policy, which justifies its higher cost relative to standard term life insurance due to the return-of-premium feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="817d0dcb-1390-42ee-b441-ff53e6769ad8">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 in total premiums reflects the cumulative payments required to qualify for the return-of-premium benefit, which justifies the higher initial cost of the policy relative to standard term life insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 return-of-premium amount is guaranteed regardless of age-related inaccuracies in application, ensuring consistent repayment conditions even if the insured misrepresented their age.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4" target="a176a4ea-8eba-4f29-8ca6-99b1da801960">
  <data key="d3">The $32,400 refundable amount corresponds directly to the final payout available when surrendering the policy after 20 years, confirming that the ROP feature enables full recovery of premiums upon timely surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dc9246f-063f-4304-84db-8fd857c1de66" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">represents</data>
</edge>
