<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">Early surrenders are evaluated relative to the policy’s expiration date; without defining when the term ends, the timeline for calculating refunds would lack reference point.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314">
  <data key="d3">The early surrender refund rules define the percentage returns over time, culminating in a 100% refund at year 20—which directly corresponds to the scenario described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d3">The varying refund percentages tied to surrender timing depend on the total premiums paid, which is quantified as $32,400 for full repayment after 20 years; thus, the refund scales are relative to this base amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 introduces the variable nature of premium returns based on surrender timing. Fact_sentence_2 provides a concrete example of this variability by specifying zero return during the first five years.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence states that the return of premium depends on when the policy is surrendered. The second sentence specifies that during Years 6–10, 30% of premiums are returned, illustrating one instance of this variable rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence states that the return of premium depends on when the policy is surrendered. The second sentence specifies that during Years 11–15, 60% of premiums are returned, illustrating one instance of the broader rule described earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence introduces a general rule about varying returns based on surrender time. The second sentence provides a concrete example of that rule’s application at the terminal point of the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence introduces a general principle that the amount returned upon surrender depends on when it occurs. The second sentence specifies that during Years 16–19, 90% of premiums are returned, illustrating the application of that principle within a particular timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the conditions under which a partial or full refund of premiums is issued when the policy is terminated early. The second sentence explains that in case of death during the term, beneficiaries receive a guaranteed death benefit regardless of surrender timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines that premature policy termination results in partial or full premium returns based on duration. This principle directly informs fact_sentence_2, where the same refund rules apply if the insured dies during the term, ensuring consistency in payout mechanics regardless of cause.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">The timing of a policy surrender determines the ROP amount; once determined, the insurer processes the refund within 60 days of the surrender event.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">The return of premium upon early surrender varies by policy duration, relying on accurate knowledge of the annual premium to calculate refunds correctly.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The condition for returning premiums when surrendering early relies on consistent premium payments; since premiums are fixed, the amount returned can be reliably calculated based on tenure.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">The return of premium upon early surrender depends on the number of years the policy has been active, which relies on consistent premium payments made according to the scheduled due dates.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The return of premium upon early surrender depends on when the surrender occurs, but only if all premiums have been paid throughout the term can the full refund be received at maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies how much of the premium is returned based on surrender timing, which directly informs the mechanism described in fact_sentence_2 about accessing cash value via surrender. Together, they clarify the financial implications of early versus late surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The timing of surrender affects the return amount under the original schedule, but reinstatement resets the eligibility clock for ROP benefits, reducing prior accumulated entitlements tied to pre-lapse tenure.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The return of premium schedule depends on surrender timing, which may be affected indirectly if a policy is reinstated, resetting certain protections like the contestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6904c391-74d9-4e98-97d5-40e29a1fdbb4" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">total_premium_paid</data>
</edge>
