</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy does not allow any premium return during its initial five years, the significance of the final maturity date—September 15, 2044—is underscored, as only after this point do full returns become possible under the ROP terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_TERM_END</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes a restriction preventing any refund in the first five years, which contextualizes why meeting the survival requirement in fact_sentence_1—after 20 years—is necessary to access the full return.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d3">No refund is available in Years 1–5 due to insufficient tenure, meaning the full $32,400 cannot be received unless the policy lasts through its full 20-year term.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS FULL PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">The absence of any premium return in Years 1–5 directly illustrates how the return of premium depends on when the policy is surrendered, supporting the conditional mechanism described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">The absence of any premium return in Years 1–5 sets the baseline condition, leading into the introduction of a 30% refund starting in Year 6, marking the transition to higher returns over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">The absence of any refund in the initial five years sets up a baseline condition; by years 11–15, the policy allows for a partial refund of 60%, reflecting progressive accumulation of return rights over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">The absence of any premium return in the initial years sets up a baseline condition that contrasts with the eventual full refund available after two decades, illustrating a cumulative escalation in benefits tied to policy duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">The absence of any premium return in the initial years sets up a baseline for understanding later increases in refund rates; the 90% return in years 16–19 reflects a significant step forward in the gradual escalation of returns outlined in the policy’s surrender provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a premium return in the initial years does not affect the consistency of annual payments. The flat premium amount remains unchanged regardless of surrender timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">The absence of premium returns in the initial five years applies when the policy is terminated voluntarily before maturity. This condition does not affect the payment of the full death benefit should the insured pass away during that period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The absence of refunds in early surrenders (Years 1–5) aligns with the principle that benefits are scaled according to duration; this same scaling applies when death occurs during the term, ensuring consistency in payout mechanics regardless of trigger event.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the lack of refund eligibility during early policy years if surrendered, while fact_sentence_2 specifies when the annual premium is due. The two statements concern separate operational rules—one about returns, the other about deadlines.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the lack of premium returns during the initial five years if the policy is surrendered. This condition depends on the cumulative premiums paid, which are determined by the fixed annual rate stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">The absence of ROP payouts in the initial five years sets a condition under which the later timeline for refunds becomes relevant. This establishes context for when the 60-day rule would apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a premium return in the initial five years depends on whether all premiums were paid; failure to pay them would disqualify even later claims. This underscores why consistent payment is essential for eventual eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that no premium return occurs in years 1–5, which supports the claim in fact_sentence_2 that early access to cash value is restricted unless the full term ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a premium return in years 1–5 may be overridden if the policy is later reinstated, as the ROP calculation excludes the lapsed period, potentially allowing earlier eligibility for returns than originally indicated.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The lack of premium return in early years (fact_sentence_1) sets baseline expectations for policy value accumulation, whereas fact_sentence_2 adds complexity by introducing a renewed contestability period upon reinstatement, affecting claim eligibility even if premiums were previously paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f58db7d1-ad49-4611-8b3b-f110c8eb014c" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">not refunded</data>
</edge>
