  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CRITICAL_NOTE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">The provision allowing a 30% refund during Years 6–10 implies that the policy extends beyond Year 5 and confirms its existence up to at least Year 10, supporting the significance of the final maturity date set for September 15, 2044.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314">
  <data key="d3">The early surrender refund percentage during Years 6–10 reflects a separate clause that operates independently of the final maturity payout. It does not influence or derive from the survivorship condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d3">The 30% refund rate applicable in Years 6–10 implies a proportional share of the total premiums ($32,400), providing context for what constitutes 100% of payments made over the policy’s duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS_TOTAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence gives an example of the surrender return rate—30% in Years 6–10—which exemplifies the broader principle stated in the first sentence that returns vary based on surrender timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS EXAMPLE OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">A 30% refund becomes applicable only after the initial non-refundable period (Years 1–5), meaning the earlier clause directly conditions when the later provision takes effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate increases from 30% in Years 6–10 to 60% in Years 11–15, reflecting a progressive improvement in surrender value as the policy ages beyond its initial decade.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">The partial refund rate of 30% in Years 6–10 sets a baseline for understanding the gradual increase in return rates, culminating in full premium repayment by Year 20.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate increases progressively over time; after Year 10, the return rises significantly beyond the 30% offered in Years 6–10, culminating in 90% returns by Years 16–19.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines partial premium repayment when the policy is surrendered between years 6 and 10. The second sentence states that beneficiaries receive the full death benefit regardless of surrender status, but it does not reference any interaction with the refund schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate specified for early surrenders in Years 6–10 applies directly to determining the proportional refund given to beneficiaries if the insured dies during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate of 30% during Years 6–10 depends on the total premiums paid, which are determined by the fixed annual premium of $1,620.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate for early surrenders in Years 6–10 depends on the total premiums paid, which are guaranteed to remain unchanged due to stable annual payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">The amount of premium refund due upon surrender in Years 6–10 is determined by the policy’s ROP schedule, and such refunds are processed within 60 days of the surrender event.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMING_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the refund amount available if the policy is surrendered between years 6 and 10. This information relies on the overall timeline of the policy but does not depend on the exact payment date specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The 30% refund during Years 6–10 applies only under the condition that all premiums have been paid throughout the policy’s duration, making it contingent on meeting the eligibility criteria outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 illustrates a concrete example of the ROP percentage applied during mid-term surrender, directly supporting the general rule stated in fact_sentence_2 about accessing cash value via surrender with ROP.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The ROP refund rate described in fact_sentence_1 depends on continuous premium payments over time, but upon reinstatement, the accumulated tenure for calculating refunds restarts, meaning earlier contributions may not count toward future returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The ROP percentage applied when surrendering during Years 6–10 may be affected if the policy was previously lapsed and later reinstated, since reinstatement triggers a new contestability period that could impact claim validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
