<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a 60% refund during Years 11–15 implies that the policy remains active beyond Year 10 and extends toward its conclusion on September 15, 2044, confirming the timeline established by the policy end date.</data>
  <data key="d4">FALLS_WITHIN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314">
  <data key="d3">The second statement explains a refund percentage (60%) offered when surrendering during middle years of the policy. This contrasts with the first statement, which covers the complete refund received solely upon survival to the maturity date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d3">The 60% refund rate applicable in Years 11–15 implies a proportional share of the total premiums ($32,400), reinforcing that this figure represents the full accumulated payments over the policy’s duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROPORTIONAL_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence gives an example of the surrender return rate during Years 11–15, where 60% of premiums are returned. This exemplifies the condition stated in the first sentence regarding variable returns based on surrender timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">While the policy offers no returns in the first five years, it evolves into providing increasingly favorable refunds—such as 60% in years 11–15—as part of its staged return mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">As the policy matures past Year 10, the surrender refund rises significantly compared to earlier periods, showing that later years offer greater financial returns than those before them.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate increases from 60% in Years 11–15 to 90% in Years 16–19, reflecting a stepwise improvement in benefits tied to longer policy tenure.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the partial premium refund available when the policy is surrendered between years 11 and 15. The second sentence specifies the guaranteed death benefit paid to beneficiaries if the insured passes away before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate rises steadily over time, with 60% returned after 11–15 years, culminating in a full 100% return by Year 20, reflecting a graduated escalation in benefits for longer-held policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate of 60% for surrenders in Years 11–15 reflects the established early surrender schedule, which also governs the proportional refunds given to beneficiaries if the insured dies during those years.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">When a policyholder surrenders during Years 11–15, they are entitled to 60% of premiums paid; this amount is disbursed by the insurer within 60 days of the surrender event.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMING_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the refund percentage applicable during mid-term surrenders; this percentage relies on the annual premium figure stated in fact_sentence_2 to determine the exact refund amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate specified in Fact Sentence 1 depends on the number of years premiums have been paid, which requires knowing the regularity and timing of those payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The 60% refund rate for surrenders in Years 11–15 relies on the assumption that annual premiums remain unchanged; without stable premiums, the refund amount could not be reliably calculated or applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The 60% refund rate applicable in Years 11–15 assumes that all required premiums have been paid throughout the policy’s duration, including up to Year 20.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 illustrates a concrete example of the ROP percentage applied during mid-term surrender, directly supporting the general rule stated in fact_sentence_2 about accessing cash value via surrender with ROP.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The ROP refund rate applicable in Years 11–15 depends on continuous coverage; if the policy lapses and later renews, the accumulated tenure used to calculate returns excludes the gap, potentially delaying access to high-return tiers even if total elapsed time exceeds Year 15.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The surrender refund rate defined in fact_sentence_1 applies only when the policy remains active; if the policy lapses and is later reinstated, the ROP terms reset, potentially altering future refund calculations. This creates an indirect link where reinstatement may impact the ability to access benefits outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
