<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">The 90% refund rate applicable in Years 16–19 implies that the policy remains active beyond Year 15 and extends toward its final maturity on September 15, 2044, confirming the significance of that endpoint.</data>
  <data key="d4">FALLS_WITHIN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314">
  <data key="d3">The 90% refund rate during Years 16–19 provides context for understanding the progression leading up to the full 100% refund detailed in fact_sentence_1, illustrating how partial returns increase over time before culminating in total repayment at maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">LEADS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d3">A 90% refund during Years 16–19 indicates substantial but incomplete recovery of premiums, consistent with the eventual 100% return ($32,400) achievable only after full 20-year tenure.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence gives an example of the surrender return rate during late policy years, reinforcing the idea introduced in the first sentence that returns vary significantly based on the timing of surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">While the early years offer zero refunds, the high 90% return available in years 16–19 highlights the cumulative nature of the ROP schedule, demonstrating that longer retention leads to substantially greater benefits compared to early termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">While the earlier period (Years 6–10) offers only a modest 30% refund, the subsequent phase (Years 16–19) reflects a substantial escalation to 90%, demonstrating a clear upward trend in premium recovery.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">As the policy duration extends beyond Year 15, the surrender refund rises significantly—from 60% in earlier years to 90%, demonstrating cumulative advantage over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">The refund rate increases from 90% in Years 16–19 to 100% by Year 20, reflecting an incremental improvement in benefits tied to longer policy duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the refund percentage when a policy is surrendered late in its term, but it does not affect or relate to the payment of the death benefit upon the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The 90% refund rate applicable during Years 16–19 for policy surrenders reflects the early surrender schedule used to determine refunds when the insured dies during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">The 90% refund rate during Years 16–19 relies on knowing the annual premium amount to compute the total premiums paid. Without the annual premium figure, the exact refund cannot be determined.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The consistent annual payment of premiums ensures that the cumulative amount eligible for refund under the early surrender schedule remains calculable and reliable across each policy year.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">The 90% refund rate for surrenders in Years 16–19 relies on the consistent annual payment schedule established by the requirement that premiums be paid each September 15.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">When a policyholder surrenders during Years 16–19, they qualify for a 90% refund of premiums paid; this refund is processed and disbursed within 60 days of the surrender event.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_WITHIN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The 90% refund during Years 16–19 applies only if all premiums have been consistently paid throughout the policy’s duration, ensuring that the policy remains active and eligible for such benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 illustrates a specific instance of the general rule outlined in fact_sentence_2: returning 90% of premiums during years 16–19 occurs via full surrender under the ROP framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The ROP return rate in years 16–19 depends on continuous coverage; if the policy lapses and is later reinstated, those prior years do not count toward the accumulation needed for high surrender returns like 90%.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The ROP provision allows high premium refunds during mid-term surrender, but reinstatement triggers a fresh contestability period, potentially affecting claim eligibility even if prior payments were made under favorable ROP terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c2fb8af2-c3dc-4c53-8a91-3ed6b90d8d79" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">return_rate_on_surrender</data>
