</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="456596a5-0247-4b68-af64-0e0aef758085">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CRITICAL_NOTE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">Receiving 100% of premiums back at Year 20 occurs because this coincides with the policy’s maturity date, meaning the policy terminates after exactly 20 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that at Year 20, 100% of premiums are returned if surrendered; this fully accounts for the outcome detailed in fact_sentence_1, where surviving to the end of the term results in receiving $32,400.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d3">The rule stating that 100% of premiums are returned at Year 20 provides context for why $32,400 is the correct total of premiums paid over the policy’s duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence illustrates the culmination of the surrender-return schedule introduced in the first sentence, showing the highest possible return percentage after 20 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">Receiving 100% of premiums back at year 20 implies that earlier surrenders, such as those in years 1–5, cannot result in refunds, making the later payout contingent on surviving through the entire term.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">Reaching 100% refund eligibility at Year 20 reflects the final stage of a cumulative escalation path initiated earlier, such as the 30% return available in Years 6–10.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">Year 20 marks the final milestone where full premium repayment occurs; prior periods like Years 11–15 offer lower returns (60%), showing that earlier surrenders result in reduced payouts compared to holding through the entire term.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">Year 20 represents the culmination of the gradual refund progression described earlier, where full premium repayment becomes available after sustained policy holding beyond Year 19.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">The first statement outlines the full premium refund available when the policy is surrendered at maturity after 20 years. The second statement explains that beneficiaries receive the full death benefit regardless of surrender status, should the insured pass away before the end of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">When the policy reaches Year 20 and is surrendered, 100% of premiums are due; this refund is processed and issued by the insurer within 60 days of the surrender event.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The full refund at Year 20 reflects the final stage of the refund schedule used for early surrenders. This same schedule governs the proportional refund given to beneficiaries if the insured dies before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXTENDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">The statement about returning 100% of premiums at Year 20 depends on knowing the annual payment amount to compute the total accumulated premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">The full refund at Year 20 requires consistent adherence to the annual payment schedule, including timely payments on September 15 each year.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The full return of premiums at Year 20 depends on having met all prior payment obligations; without consistent premium payments, the 100% refund cannot be received.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The full refund at Year 20 depends on consistent payment of fixed premiums; without stable, unchanging annual premiums, the accumulation of the required sum would not be guaranteed.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The 100% premium return at year 20 assumes continuous coverage without lapse, which could be disrupted if reinstatement occurs, triggering a new contestability period affecting claim eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder lets the policy lapse and later reinstates it, the 100% return condition depends on completing a fresh 20-year period from reinstatement onward, effectively resetting the eligibility clock.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 illustrates a key instance of the mechanism described in fact_sentence_2: the full return of premiums at Year 20 corresponds exactly to accessing cash value via surrender under the ROP schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2181043b-4d33-40d9-a54b-802ff0211aa4" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">returned_at_maturity</data>
</edge>
