<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="cd1ad5bf-716a-4727-9553-806be53f7978">
  <data key="d3">The provision for paying the full death benefit requires that the insured dies while the policy is still active. This activity period is bounded by the policy’s termination date, set for September 15, 2044.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="9d6e8c8d-386c-4d95-828f-985897635314">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the death benefit received by beneficiaries if the insured dies during the policy term, contrasting with fact_sentence_1’s scenario where the policyholder gets a premium refund after surviving to maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE OUTCOME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="c58f2abb-08d5-4d9b-8e01-36501b9318c4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the guaranteed death benefit received by beneficiaries when the insured dies before maturity. It stands independent of the premium refund calculation detailed in fact_sentence_1, which applies only to surviving policyholders.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence specifies the death benefit entitlement upon the insured's passing during the policy term. This scenario is separate from early surrender; however, it shares the same underlying mechanism for calculating refunds via the early surrender scale, though applied differently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">Receiving the full $300,000 death benefit upon the insured’s passing is guaranteed regardless of whether premiums were returned earlier. The timing of premium refunds, such as none in the first five years, does not influence this outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence specifies the guaranteed death benefit payment upon the insured’s passing during the term. This outcome is independent of whether the policy was surrendered earlier or what percentage of premiums would have been refunded under such circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence establishes the death benefit entitlement regardless of surrender conditions. The first sentence details the financial outcome if the policy is terminated by surrender rather than through death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence specifies that beneficiaries get the full death benefit regardless of surrender terms, meaning the refund rate applicable to early surrenders does not impact this payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">The second statement specifies the death benefit entitlement for beneficiaries in case of premature death. This does not affect or rely on the condition described in the first statement about returning premiums at year 20 upon surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326">
  <data key="d3">The receipt of the full death benefit is augmented by a proportional refund of premiums when death occurs during the term, determined using the early surrender schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">The receipt of the death benefit triggers the timeline for processing related Return of Premium (ROP) payments, ensuring benefits are disbursed promptly after the claim event.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit of $300,000 is available only if the policy remains in force, which depends on timely premium payments such as the $1,620 annual installment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The receipt of the $300,000 death benefit by beneficiaries is unaffected by whether premiums remain level. This fact stands independently of premium payment consistency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit provision ensures that beneficiaries receive $300,000 if the insured dies before maturity, independent of when premiums are paid. The requirement for an annual premium due on September 15 supports ongoing coverage but does not affect the death benefit eligibility directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the death benefit payout upon premature termination due to death, independent of premium repayment status beyond what's required by contract. The second sentence establishes eligibility criteria for returning premiums only if all payments were made over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">The 20-year term guarantees eligibility for the full $300,000 death benefit only when the insured dies before the end of the term, linking the payout directly to the policy’s lifespan.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">The second fact states that beneficiaries get the full $300,000 death benefit if the insured dies within the term, which is consistent with and supported by the details in the first fact about the policy’s coverage and payout structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit of $300,000 is paid when the insured dies before the end of the term, while survival beyond the term leads to a complete refund of all premiums paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">A death benefit of $300,000 is paid to beneficiaries if the insured dies during the term, whereas surviving the term triggers a return of $32,400 in premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_OUTCOME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the death benefit entitlement of $300,000 when the insured dies before the end of the term, which depends on having fulfilled the required premium obligations detailed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 affirms that beneficiaries get the full $300,000 if death occurs during the term, supporting and reinforcing the key provision stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="e8f2bfea-e66b-488f-86a1-43ceaf048efd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 supports fact_sentence_1 by confirming the payment of the full death benefit, which serves as the foundation for the additional refund mentioned in fact_sentence_1 under the ROP framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="56d974f0-7976-40f7-a400-a08ec69d94ac">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains the conditions under which the $300,000 death benefit is paid, which is consistent with and supported by fact_sentence_1 stating the benefit amount outright.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">The promise of a $300,000 payout upon death during the term reinforces why the policy’s end date in fact_sentence_1 is significant—it marks the final moment before the policy lapses without triggering any further claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 death benefit depends on consistent payment of the $1,620 annual premium; without it, the benefit would not be available upon the insured's passing during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 details the outcome if the insured dies within the term, which contrasts with fact_sentence_1's scenario but aligns logically since both cover distinct endpoints of the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
