  <data key="d3">The proportional refund rule applied upon death relies on the total premiums paid ($32,400) being known, ensuring accurate calculation according to the established schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS ON TOTAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that upon death during the term, beneficiaries get a proportional refund via the early surrender schedule. This mirrors the condition described in fact_sentence_1, showing that the refund rule applies not only to voluntary surrenders but also to involuntary terminations due to death.</data>
  <data key="d4">BASED ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">When death happens during the term, beneficiaries get a partial refund tied to the early surrender schedule, reinforcing that even without surrender, the time-based refund rule governs returns, including cases like premature termination via death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">The early surrender refund schedule, including the 30% rate for Years 6–10, governs the amount refunded when the policyholder dies before maturity, ensuring consistency across payout types.</data>
  <data key="d4">GOVERNS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiaries receiving a proportional refund upon death during the term rely on the same early surrender schedule referenced in the 60% refund applicable to surrenders in Years 11–15.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">The proportional refund for death benefits uses the same early surrender schedule referenced in the 90% refund rate for surrenders in Years 16–19.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiaries receiving a proportional refund due to death use the same refund percentage scale applied when a policyholder surrenders after 20 years and gets 100% back.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="8f9837c0-a23e-4f57-9edf-a1e053c7fa11">
  <data key="d3">A proportional refund of premiums is granted alongside the full death benefit if the insured dies during the term, reflecting the policy’s refund mechanism tied to duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXTENDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="aef30bb1-b272-4deb-bbc2-68ebbf16702a">
  <data key="d3">The proportional refund due to beneficiaries upon death relies on the early surrender schedule; this refund is processed and disbursed within 60 days of the death event.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="42e69377-0625-4ae5-a39b-739f702ac7a7">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit includes a refund of premiums based on tenure, but this is independent of when the annual premium is due.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="3426c616-0275-4cec-9ecd-43426037d96e">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiaries receive a proportional refund if the insured dies during the term, calculated using the early surrender schedule. This refund relies on total premiums paid, which depend on the known annual premium rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="52b46745-e979-474e-98c8-d03bf1b89c96">
  <data key="d3">The proportional refund for death benefits relies on consistent premium payments; since premiums are fixed, the calculation of the refund remains reliable and aligned with the early surrender schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">The refund amount beneficiaries receive when the insured dies during the term depends on whether all premiums have been paid; failure to pay all premiums reduces the refund eligibility, aligning with the requirement stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">The early surrender refund mechanism relies on the 20-year term framework, making the term duration essential for determining refund eligibility and amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">The second fact elaborates on the financial outcome for beneficiaries upon death during the term, confirming that it includes a partial refund of premiums tied to the policy’s duration—a key feature implied but not detailed in the first fact's summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPANDS_UPON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">While the second fact addresses partial premium returns when death happens before the end of the term, it complements the first by showing that even in such cases, some portion of premiums may still be recovered under the defined refund scale.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIES_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that beneficiaries get a proportionate refund of premiums when death occurs during the term; this refund is calculated relative to the total premiums paid, which is explicitly stated as $32,400 in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces conditional premium refunds upon early death, which complements fact_sentence_1’s scenario of full refund only when surviving the entire term, showing a unified refund framework regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="cf7084aa-de51-4c4d-b872-2f550bc9320d">
  <data key="d3">While the core death benefit remains unchanged, its actual amount increases due to a supplementary refund of premiums calculated under the early surrender schedule applicable at time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="56d974f0-7976-40f7-a400-a08ec69d94ac">
  <data key="d3">While the core death benefit is $300,000, it is augmented by a refund of a portion of premiums based on how many years the policy had been in force prior to death.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS_BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="e8f2bfea-e66b-488f-86a1-43ceaf048efd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that beneficiaries get a proportionate refund upon death, which supports fact_sentence_1’s assertion that such refunds are paid in addition to the death benefit, validating its accuracy within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains the refund mechanism triggered when death occurs before the policy's end date, making the specific end date in fact_sentence_1 essential for calculating eligibility and amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The provision for a proportionate premium refund upon death during the term depends entirely on the known annual premium amount of $1,620, ensuring accurate computation of benefits based on duration of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CALCULATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c89f0a7a-2453-4e9c-bef6-3c474f56b326" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">While the first fact outlines the maximum refund available after full-term survival, it implicitly relies on the framework established in the second fact—that refunds depend on tenure—and thus supports understanding the conditional nature of payouts regardless of outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
