  <data key="d3">The annual premium amount of $1,620 must be paid on the specified deadline each year. This ensures timely fulfillment of the policy’s payment requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DUE_DATE_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium being set at $1,620 implies consistency in cost, ensuring it does not fluctuate across years. This fixed rate supports the claim that premiums remain level throughout the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">LEVELS WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium amount of $1,620 sets the baseline financial requirement that may be paid within a 31-day grace period if due dates are missed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the annual premium amount ($1,620) enables the policyholder to understand what must be paid consistently to meet the eligibility criteria for the full return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay the $1,620 annual premium creates a condition under which failure to do so within any applicable grace period results in policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The $1,620 annual premium must be paid on time to maintain eligibility for the return-of-premium benefit. Failure to pay results in loss of this benefit if the policy lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium amount does not influence the availability of conversion privileges based on age. Conversion eligibility depends solely on reaching or being under age 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The $1,620 annual premium sets the baseline financial obligation whose timely payment determines eligibility for the full return-of-premium benefit. Late payment triggers a 10% reduction in that benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay $1,620 annually creates a binding obligation where failure to meet it results in irreversible consequences, such as losing the return-of-premium benefit. Since missed premiums cannot be made up, adherence to the schedule is essential.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium of $1,620 defines the cost of maintaining coverage, while the availability of conversion before expiration provides flexibility in policy management. These elements exist independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
