  <data key="d3">The requirement that the annual premium be paid on September 15 ensures compliance with the schedule needed to maintain eligibility for the full return of premiums at maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the annual premium be paid on September 15 aligns with the condition that premiums remain unchanged throughout the term, ensuring predictable yearly obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the required payment date, and fact_sentence_2 provides a leniency window allowing a delay of up to 31 days beyond that date without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
