  <data key="d3">Because premiums are guaranteed to stay level over the term, each year’s payment will exactly match the stated annual amount of $1,620.</data>
  <data key="d4">FIXED AT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums are guaranteed to stay level across the term, the consistent due date of September 15 ensures stable, recurring financial commitments without variation.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">The consistency of premium amounts across the term ensures predictability in financial obligations, which complements the inclusion of a grace period offering temporary relief from strict deadlines.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The level nature of premiums ensures stable, predictable payments, making it easier for the policyholder to meet the on-time payment requirement necessary for the full return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The level nature of premiums ensures predictability in financial commitment, making it easier for the policyholder to maintain timely payments. Failure to do so results in losing the return-of-premium benefit, highlighting how payment consistency tied to fixed premiums determines the retention of this feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums implies consistent financial obligations, which underpin the requirement to make timely payments. Failure to do so—even once—can trigger policy lapse, making regular payment adherence essential despite stable rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIES CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium amount ensures predictability, but because missed payments cannot be restored, policyholders face immediate penalties if they fail to pay on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">The consistency of premium amounts ensures predictable cost over time, supporting long-term planning. This stability indirectly enables continued eligibility for benefits like conversion, though it doesn't influence the availability of conversion itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">The consistency of premium amounts ensures predictable cost over time, while the ability to convert to permanent insurance provides flexibility later in the term. These features operate independently but contribute to overall policy design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The consistent, unchanging nature of premiums ensures predictability in financial commitment, which underpins the requirement for punctual payments necessary to preserve the full return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums indicates financial predictability across the policy term. This does not affect or influence the timing or conditions under which conversion privileges may be exercised.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence states that premiums remain unchanged throughout the term. This information does not provide context for or influence the second sentence regarding the minimum conversion amount.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums ensures financial predictability across the term but does not influence or depend on the deadline for exercising the conversion privilege.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes that premiums stay fixed throughout the term. This information does not influence or relate to the second sentence's detail about the upper limit of $300,000 for converting to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">The constancy of premiums over the term ensures predictable cost management but has no bearing on the maximum amount available for converting to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">The original policy maintains fixed premiums over its term, ensuring predictability. Upon conversion to permanent insurance, however, the new premium adjusts according to the insured’s attained age, reflecting updated risk assessment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums describes consistent payment obligations, while the prohibition on policy loans addresses limitations on borrowing against the policy’s value. These are independent structural constraints within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">The stability of premiums over time allows policyholders to plan ahead, making it feasible to consider conversion options later in the term, knowing costs won’t rise. This predictability sets the stage for understanding that any such conversion comes with trade-offs, like losing the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">The statement about level premiums emphasizes consistent payment obligations, while the prohibition on partial withdrawals underscores limited access to funds. These points reflect separate structural features of the policy but do not influence one another directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">The consistent, unchanging nature of premiums ensures predictability in financial commitment, but when the policyholder converts it into permanent insurance, any accumulated premiums are lost since the return-of-premium feature terminates.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">The stable, level premiums ensure consistent eligibility for the return-of-premium benefit, which determines whether the policyholder can access cash value upon surrender or at maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">A stable premium schedule is essential for fulfilling the terms of the Return of Premium feature, ensuring the policyholder qualifies for the complete refund of all paid premiums after surviving the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">A consistent 20-year term allows for guaranteed level premiums, making long-term financial planning feasible under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">Consistent, unchanging premiums make it possible for the insured to pay all required amounts on time, thereby fulfilling the condition necessary for the full return of premiums outlined in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the total premiums paid allows verification that the level premium structure has been consistently maintained, confirming no increases occurred over the 20 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Level premiums ensure predictable cost management, enabling the policyholder to reliably pay all premiums and thus qualify for the $32,400 return upon surviving the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The confirmation that premiums do not increase supports the accuracy of the $1,620 annual figure cited in the first fact, ensuring long-term affordability and plan integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of level premiums ensures that the annual payment model stated in fact_sentence_1 remains stable and unchanged throughout the entire term of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed return of $32,400 hinges on paying the same $1,620 annually for 20 years, so stable premiums ensure eligibility for the full refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205" target="5875c040-ac0c-4e62-bbe3-c3cc925fe67d">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of level premiums ensures predictable cost management from the start date of September 15, 2024, enabling accurate planning based on the initial policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
