<edge source="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a requirement necessary for fact_sentence_1’s outcome: timely premium payments ensure eligibility for the $32,400 return, making it a prerequisite for realizing the financial benefit described.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec" target="5875c040-ac0c-4e62-bbe3-c3cc925fe67d">
  <data key="d3">Timely payment of premiums beginning from the issuance date ensures eligibility for the full return of premiums, making the original issue date critical to fulfilling that condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments ensure eligibility for the full return of premiums upon term completion, which is one of the two primary ways to access cash value as described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder misses a premium payment leading to a lapse, they may still reinstate coverage within five years, but doing so does not restore eligibility for the original return-of-premium benefit unless all past obligations are met and the timeline restarts.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make timely premium payments results in loss of the return-of-premium benefit and may lead to policy lapse, necessitating reinstatement under specific conditions including proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid on time, the policy may lapse, requiring reinstatement under specific terms—including paying overdue amounts with interest—as outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid on time, the policy may lapse, preventing the return of premiums. However, reinstatement is possible within five years if the insured survives, allowing the policy to resume under modified terms including reset ROP calculations and a new contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make timely premium payments may cause policy lapse, requiring reinstatement, which initiates a new two-year suicide and contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are missed but the policy is later reinstated, the requirement for full ROP still applies going forward, but the returned amount excludes the lapsed period, effectively resetting the timeline for qualification.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
