  <data key="d3">The availability of a 31-day grace period allows for delayed payment of the $1,620 annual premium without immediate penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period implies flexibility around the fixed September 15 due date established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a 31-day grace period allows policyholders some leeway in making timely payments, supporting the overall reliability of meeting fixed premium requirements despite occasional delays.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period enables policyholders to avoid forfeiting the full return if they miss the exact due date, thereby supporting compliance with the on-time payment condition required by the return-of-premium clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 introduces a 31-day grace period allowing delayed payment. Fact sentence 2 states that failure to pay during this period results in policy lapse, completing the cause-effect chain.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows policyholders to avoid lapsing if they miss the deadline, thereby preventing the forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit described in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS FORFEITURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows late payment without immediate termination, but any such payment still incurs a 10% reduction in the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 mentions a 31-day grace period for premium payments, suggesting leniency. Fact sentence 2 contradicts this by stating that missed premiums cannot be recovered, meaning even if paid during the grace period, they do not restore eligibility for the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate penalty, while the conversion option enables transitioning to permanent coverage later. These are independent benefits not logically dependent on each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payment without immediate penalty, supporting continued eligibility for benefits like the return-of-premium feature. This does not directly affect the availability of conversion privileges, which remain independent of payment timeliness.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows some leeway in making timely premium payments but does not affect the minimum conversion amount required for switching to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows some leeway in making timely payments, but it does not affect the deadlines tied to the conversion privilege described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate penalty, but it does not affect the maximum conversion amount available under the policy’s conversion privilege.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payment within 31 days without penalty, supporting continued coverage while maintaining compliance requirements. This does not affect the availability of conversion benefits before age 65, which depends solely on reaching that milestone.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payment without immediate penalty, but it does not affect the calculation of future premiums after conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate penalty, while the maximum conversion amount being tied to the current face value defines the upper bound of what can be converted into permanent insurance. These features operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows flexibility in meeting payment deadlines, helping maintain eligibility for the return-of-premium benefit. This indirectly supports continued qualification for benefits before any potential conversion decision.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows some leniency in paying premiums on time, while the prohibition on policy loans restricts borrowing against the policy's value. These rules independently govern payment flexibility and financial access.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payment without immediate penalty, maintaining eligibility for future returns if corrected. However, even if payments are eventually made after the grace period, converting the policy results in complete forfeiture of previously paid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO IMPACT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows some leniency in paying premiums on time, but it has no direct connection to the restriction against partial withdrawals, which governs how cash value may be accessed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payments without immediate penalty, potentially affecting whether a payment qualifies as 'on time' and thus impacts eligibility for the full return-of-premium benefit described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
