  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the $1,620 annual premium within the grace period triggers policy lapse, meaning the financial commitment outlined in the first sentence was not fulfilled.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay the annual premium by September 15 exists to prevent the policy from lapsing upon nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapping due to unpaid premiums highlights why consistent payment discipline matters even when premiums are fixed. Since premiums don’t change over time, missing one becomes more impactful relative to predictable cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS ON TIMELINESS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The need to make all payments on time to secure the full return depends on avoiding a lapse, which occurs if a premium isn't paid during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 describes the outcome of missing the grace period: policy lapse. This depends directly on the existence of the grace period mentioned in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period leads to policy lapse, which triggers the termination of the return-of-premium benefit. This shows how payment delinquency cascades into loss of financial advantage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period triggers policy lapse, making any subsequent attempt to recover the missed premium impossible due to the policy's rules against reinstatement after default.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">A late payment during the grace period triggers a 10% reduction in the return-of-premium benefit. This condition occurs before the point where failure to pay leads to lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period results in policy lapse, which would eliminate eligibility for any future benefits including conversion to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period results in policy lapse, terminating coverage. Conversion availability depends solely on timing relative to expiration, independent of payment history.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the grace period leads to policy lapse, but this does not directly relate to the minimum conversion amount required when exercising the conversion privilege.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the grace period results in policy lapse, potentially eliminating future options like conversion. This outcome could prevent someone from exercising the conversion privilege before age 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums within the grace period results in policy lapse, terminating coverage. This outcome may prevent the individual from meeting the deadline for converting to permanent insurance, especially if it occurs close to age 65 or policy expiry.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the grace period results in policy lapse, but this has no bearing on the maximum allowable conversion amount of $300,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the grace period leads to policy lapse, terminating coverage. This does not directly affect the maximum conversion amount, which depends solely on the current face value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period results in policy lapse, but this does not directly affect the calculation of future premiums should conversion occur later. Conversion depends on timing and eligibility, independent of past payment status beyond maintaining active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period results in policy lapse, but this does not affect the prohibition on policy loans, which is independently stated as a fixed restriction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period leads to policy lapse, but this does not affect the rule about forfeiting past premiums upon conversion. Conversion triggers a distinct outcome unrelated to payment timeliness.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period causes the policy to lapse, terminating coverage. This does not directly affect the conversion privilege unless the policy has already lapsed before conversion is attempted.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the grace period leads to policy lapse, which affects coverage continuity. This does not influence the restriction on partial withdrawals, which is a separate rule governing cash value access.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period causes the policy to lapse, eliminating the possibility of accessing cash value through surrender or receiving the full return at maturity, thereby invalidating the scenarios described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES LOSS OF ACCESS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
