  <data key="d3">Lapse due to unpaid premium leads to forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, meaning timely payment of the $1,620 annual premium is essential to preserve this feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">Lapse due to unpaid premium leads to loss of the return-of-premium benefit, underscoring the importance of timely payment on September 15 annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">Forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit occurs when premiums are not paid, underscoring the importance of maintaining regular payments. This reliance on punctual payments implies that stable, unchanging premiums help ensure compliance and thus preservation of the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit occurs when the policy lapses from unpaid premiums, meaning failure to fulfill the obligation described in fact_sentence_1 causes the outcome in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make a premium payment within the 31-day grace period results in policy lapse, which triggers the forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit mentioned earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES LAPSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit occurs specifically when the policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, highlighting that delayed payment initiates the consequence described in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">A missed premium triggers immediate forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, and since such payments cannot be made up, the consequence is irreversible.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums results in forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not affect the right to convert the policy into permanent insurance later, assuming eligibility conditions like age or expiration remain met.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">A failed payment leading to policy lapse completely eliminates the return-of-premium benefit, which is a stronger condition than a late payment that only reduces it by 10%. This implies that lapsed policies represent a more serious breach than those with delayed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay premiums results in forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not affect the availability of conversion privileges before age 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums results in loss of the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not directly affect the deadline for exercising the conversion privilege.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, which may influence timing decisions around conversion. Conversion availability allows policyholders to switch plans before expiration, potentially avoiding future payment obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS_LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums results in losing the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not affect the maximum conversion amount available under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums results in forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not relate directly to the minimum conversion amount required for switching policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums results in losing the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not affect the maximum amount available upon converting to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">The first statement explains that failing to pay premiums results in losing the return-of-premium benefit. This does not directly influence the second statement, which concerns how converted policies' premiums are determined by the insured's age at conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">A failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse and forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, similar to how converting the policy terminates that benefit regardless of payment history.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums results in losing the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not affect the restriction against partial withdrawals, which applies regardless of payment history.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">The first statement explains the penalty for failing to pay premiums, specifically losing the return-of-premium benefit if the policy lapses. This does not relate directly to the unavailability of policy loans mentioned in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">The first statement explains that failing to pay premiums leads to losing the return-of-premium benefit. This contrasts with the second statement, which specifies that even if the policy is converted, past premiums are still not refunded, highlighting another scenario where refunds do not occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses from unpaid premiums, it loses its return-of-premium benefit, meaning the only remaining options for accessing cash value are either full surrender (at a reduced rate based on past delays) or surviving until the end of the term for full payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make any premium payment leads to losing the right to receive returned premiums, thus undermining the condition set forth in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS_IF_NOT_PAID</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reinforces the requirement stated in fact_sentence_1 by clarifying that any lapse in premium payment nullifies the return of premium, thus ensuring consistency with the original promise.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">A 20-year term enables the return-of-premium feature, but its availability is conditional upon uninterrupted premium payments throughout the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to maintain premium payments, as outlined in fact_sentence_2, nullifies the guaranteed return of premiums promised in fact_sentence_1, creating a direct dependency.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS_BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Failure to maintain timely premium payments, as noted in fact_sentence_2, nullifies the $32,400 return promised in fact_sentence_1, making the outcome dependent on adherence to payment terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Without consistent premium payments, the survival-based refund specified in fact_sentence_1 cannot be received, rendering the benefit conditional on adherence to payment terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS_BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the $1,620 annual premium results in forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, making timely payment essential to realizing the policy’s financial advantage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make the required annual premium payment jeopardizes the return-of-premium benefit, undermining the financial incentive outlined in the initial statement about annual billing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit mentioned in fact_sentence_1, meaning the financial incentive tied to surviving the term depends entirely on consistent payment compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="5875c040-ac0c-4e62-bbe3-c3cc925fe67d">
  <data key="d3">Failure to maintain timely premium payments after the initial issuance on September 15, 2024, results in loss of the return-of-premium benefit, directly linking the consequence to the policy’s effective start date.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">The inability to retain the return of premium benefit upon lapse contradicts the possibility of reinstating the policy later, since reinstatement does not restore previously forfeited benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The inability to maintain timely premium payment causes forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, but reinstating the policy after lapse allows restoration of coverage—if insurability is proven and conditions met.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to forfeiture of the return of premium benefit, meaning the only remaining path to receive cash value is through full surrender after a lapse—which reduces the amount received—or surviving until term end. This aligns with the restriction described in fact_sentence_2 about access methods being conditional on maintaining coverage status.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">The inability to reclaim the return of premium benefit after lapse directly impacts the viability of reinstatement, since reinstating the policy cannot reverse the forfeiture caused by unpaid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">The inability to retain the return-of-premium benefit upon lapse directly informs why reinstatement alone does not restore that benefit, even when back premiums are paid with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of the return of premium benefit upon lapse is mitigated if the policyholder reinstates coverage within the grace period, allowing the ROP calculation to reset and exclude the inactive period.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_CONSEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to maintain timely premium payments to retain the return of premium benefit underscores why the policy incurs higher costs—it guarantees future refunds under specific conditions, increasing insurer risk and thus pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_REASON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">Failure to maintain timely premium payments results in forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, but if the policy is later reinstated, it triggers a new two-year suicide and contestability period, introducing fresh underwriting risks despite restored coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
