<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">Because missed premiums cannot be made up, the fixed annual premium of $1,620 becomes non-negotiable in practice—any delay or omission directly jeopardizes the entire return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">MANDATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">Because missed premiums cannot be made up, it is essential to meet the September 15 payment deadline annually to maintain eligibility for the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">Since missed premiums cannot be made up, the requirement for consistently paying the same level premium becomes strictly enforced over the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The inability to make up missed premiums means that failing to pay on time directly prevents qualification for the full return of premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 asserts that missed premiums cannot be made up, rendering the grace period irrelevant since no action can revive a delinquent payment. Thus, the presence of a grace period has no practical effect given the absolute prohibition on recovering missed premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">NULLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">Because missed premiums cannot be made up, failing to pay within the grace period inevitably results in policy lapse, eliminating future benefits including return of premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS_RECOVERY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The inability to make up missed premiums ensures that any lapse in payment permanently eliminates eligibility for the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">A late premium payment reduces the return-of-premium benefit by 10%, reflecting a lesser penalty compared to outright miss. Since missed premiums cannot be recovered, this highlights a distinction between temporary delinquency and complete default.</data>
  <data key="d4">WORSE_THAN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">Missing premiums forfeits the return-of-premium benefit, but this restriction does not impact the timing or eligibility for converting to permanent insurance before age 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">Missing premiums leads to forfeiture of the return benefit, but does not affect the deadline for exercising the conversion privilege. Conversion eligibility depends solely on age or policy expiration date, independent of payment history.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">Missing premiums cannot be made up, meaning any lapse results in immediate loss of benefits. This restriction does not affect the minimum required amount for converting to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Missing premiums results in loss of the return-of-premium benefit, but does not affect the maximum conversion amount available under the policy’s conversion privilege.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">Missing premiums cannot be made up, meaning any lapse results in irreversible loss of benefits. This restriction does not affect the maximum conversion amount available under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">The inability to make up missed premiums relates to financial penalties and loss of return-on-premium benefits but does not affect the availability of converting the policy to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">The inability to make up missed premiums ensures strict adherence to payment schedules, while the availability of conversion before expiration provides flexibility in policy options, independent of payment history.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">Missing premiums forfeits the return-of-premium benefit, but does not affect the ability to convert to permanent insurance if done before age 65. However, once converted, the new premium rate reflects the insured's older age.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">Missing a premium means it cannot be restored, and if the policy is later converted, even the premiums already paid are lost due to termination of the return feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS RETURN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that missed premiums cannot be recovered, reinforcing strict adherence to payment schedules. This restriction operates independently from the prohibition on policy loans described in sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">Missing premiums eliminates eligibility for the return-of-premium benefit, just as conversion does. Both scenarios terminate the benefit but through different pathways—one due to non-compliance, the other due to structural change.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">Missing premiums cannot be corrected, enforcing strict adherence to payment deadlines. This restriction operates independently from the prohibition on partial withdrawals, which limits how cash value may be accessed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Missing premiums eliminates the possibility of receiving any return of premium, thereby restricting cash value access solely to full surrender after penalty application or waiting until term completion. This limitation arises because non-payment voids the return benefit entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS ACCESS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18e2e312-ded6-4abe-a1fd-b2dbba80ff9d" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Must be paid by deadline</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b15a4fd7-b43e-4107-8566-414228506952" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Deadline for payment without recovery option</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bacd46fa-fed9-4bba-8fe8-289c6639abca" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Non-recoverable if unpaid on schedule</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6fa0b1e2-7c35-431d-bb7a-089e28b1b648" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Conditional on timely full payment</data>
</edge>
