<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">A 10% reduction in the return-of-premium benefit occurs when a $1,620 annual premium is not paid on time, meaning the premium amount defines the basis for the penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">A late premium payment reduces the return-of-premium benefit by 10%, meaning timely payment on September 15 is essential to preserve the full benefit, reinforcing the importance of meeting the stated due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">Late payment penalties depend on the existence of fixed, non-increasing premiums; if premiums were variable, the impact of delay might differ significantly.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the return-of-premium benefit by 10% occurs when a premium is paid late, reinforcing the necessity of on-time payments outlined in the initial eligibility rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Late payment during the grace period results in a 10% reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, implying the grace period permits delays under specific consequences.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period results in policy lapse, which nullifies any future benefits including the return-of-premium. Late payments do not lead to lapse but incur penalties instead.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">Late payment triggers a 10% reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, serving as a lesser penalty compared to the full forfeiture caused by a lapse due to unpaid premiums, thus illustrating a graduated consequence system based on severity of default.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">Missing a premium completely prevents any return of premiums, making it worse than a late payment, which only triggers a 10% reduction. Therefore, timely action—even within a grace period—is critical to preserving benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">LESS_SEVERE_THAN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">Late payment of a premium reduces the return-of-premium benefit by 10%, but this does not affect the ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance without medical proof.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">Late payment of a premium triggers a 10% reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, independent of when conversion might occur. Conversion availability depends solely on remaining policy duration and age limits, unaffected by payment history.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments trigger a reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not relate to the minimum conversion amount required when switching policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments trigger a reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not affect the availability of conversion rights. Conversion eligibility depends solely on age and timing relative to policy expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments affect the return-of-premium benefit but have no bearing on the deadline for converting to permanent insurance. The timing of conversion depends solely on age or policy expiration, independent of payment history.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments trigger a reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not influence the maximum amount available upon converting to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">Late payment affects the return-of-premium benefit but does not influence the pricing mechanism of a future converted policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments trigger a reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not relate to the maximum amount that can be converted into permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">A late premium payment reduces the return-of-premium benefit by 10%, serving as a financial penalty. In contrast, converting the policy terminates the return-of-premium benefit entirely, regardless of timely payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">Late payment affects the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not relate to the availability of policy loans, which are prohibited regardless of payment history.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">Late payment triggers a reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not affect whether premiums are refunded upon conversion, which depends solely on the act of conversion itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments trigger a reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, but this does not affect the restriction against partial withdrawals, which applies regardless of payment timeliness.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments reduce the return-of-premium benefit by 10%, which impacts the final payout when accessing cash value either through surrender or at maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="2972655d-04e5-4677-b08a-0b7dec9c8258">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a restriction that undermines the outcome described in fact_sentence_1: even if all premiums are eventually paid, a late payment invalidates full ROP eligibility, thereby weakening the guarantee stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a penalty on delayed payments that undermines the full return guarantee mentioned in fact_sentence_1, thereby limiting its practical application unless all premiums are paid on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES_REWARD</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">A 20-year term allows for the return of all premiums if paid on time, but this benefit is diminished if even one premium is delayed beyond the grace period, making the term's success dependent on punctual payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">A delayed premium payment diminishes the guaranteed return of all premiums, meaning the promise in fact_sentence_1—that 100% of premiums will be refunded—is conditional on punctual payments, as clarified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies conditions under which the return of premiums may be diminished, directly influencing whether the $32,400 mentioned in fact_sentence_1 is fully recoverable.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS_OUTCOME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">A late premium payment triggers a reduction in the return of premium benefit, meaning the guaranteed $32,400 payout from fact_sentence_1 may not be realized unless all premiums are paid on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES_BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">A failure to pay the $1,620 premium on time results in a penalty reducing the return-of-premium benefit, meaning the initial premium figure becomes subject to adjustment based on payment timeliness.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">Since the return-of-premium benefit depends on timely annual payments, the nature of the premium being annual—highlighted in fact_sentence_1—is essential to understanding when and how the penalty in fact_sentence_2 applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 modifies the outcome stated in fact_sentence_1 by reducing the return amount when premiums are not paid on time, thereby limiting the guaranteed $32,400 payout under certain circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="5875c040-ac0c-4e62-bbe3-c3cc925fe67d">
  <data key="d3">A late premium payment during the grace period reduces the return-of-premium benefit by 10%, meaning timely payment on or before September 15, 2024—the policy’s issue date—is critical to preserving the full payout, thus grounding the consequence in the original issuance timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments trigger a 10% reduction in the return of premium benefit, which directly impacts the amount received upon full surrender—the primary method of accessing cash value outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">A late premium payment reduces the return-of-premium benefit, potentially leading to policy lapse; if that occurs, reinstatement becomes necessary and requires proof of insurability under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments reduce the return-of-premium benefit, potentially leading to lapse if unpaid long enough; reinstatement eligibility later allows recovery, but does not restore previously lost ROP reductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments trigger a penalty to the return-of-premium benefit, but reinstatement eligibility depends on the insured surviving past the lapse, meaning survival is necessary before any recovery of benefits becomes possible.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">A late premium payment reduces the return of premium benefit by 10%, while reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying overdue amounts with 6% interest. Both involve penalties for delayed payments but apply at different lifecycle points: one during the grace period, the other after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments reduce the ROP benefit by 10%, but if the policy is later reinstated, the ROP calculation excludes the lapsed period, potentially restoring some portion of the original benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">Late premium payments reduce the return of premium benefit, whereas reinstatement triggers a new two-year suicide and contestability period, introducing additional risk-based restrictions that apply independently of payment history.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The penalty for late premium payments diminishes the return-on-premium benefit, reinforcing why the policy commands a higher price than standard term life insurance—the added cost reflects both the promise of returning premiums and the risk mitigation through conditional enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52ae329f-2ad2-42d7-a005-1985aef37604" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is subject to late payment penalty</data>
</edge>
