<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">The availability of converting to permanent insurance without medical proof enhances the policy’s flexibility, but this benefit does not affect the required $1,620 annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The option to convert to permanent insurance without medical proof depends on maintaining active coverage, which relies on consistent premium payments such as those required on September 15.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The option to convert to permanent coverage without medical proof enhances long-term planning, regardless of whether premiums stay level. This feature does not rely on premium constancy for its existence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a conversion privilege allows policyholders to switch to permanent coverage without medical exams. This right exists regardless of whether premiums were paid on time, but it terminates the return-of-premium feature if exercised.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance does not rely on the existence of a grace period, nor does it affect how timely payments are handled.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">The right to convert to permanent insurance assumes the policy remains active, so it cannot apply if the policy has lapsed due to unpaid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The option to convert to permanent insurance without medical proof exists regardless of payment history, although such conversions terminate the return-of-premium feature, making it irrelevant if the policy has already lapsed due to nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without medical proof applies regardless of past payment history, meaning it operates independently of whether premiums were missed or not.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The option to convert to permanent insurance without medical proof exists regardless of whether premiums were paid late, although such delays impact the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert without medical proof applies specifically within the window before the policy's expiration date, ensuring flexibility under defined conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without medical proof is limited to policies where the insured has not yet reached age 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance is permitted without medical underwriting, and the maximum coverage available through such conversion is capped at $300,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_LIMIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance is permitted without medical proof, subject to a minimum conversion amount of $50,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_CONVERSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance is permitted without medical proof, but it must occur before the later of age 65 or policy expiration. This ensures the right is exercised within defined limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance is permitted without medical evidence, allowing flexibility in transitioning coverage. The converted policy’s maximum benefit is capped at the existing face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">Converting to permanent insurance eliminates the need for medical underwriting, but the resulting premium depends on the insured's current age at the time of conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy to permanent insurance eliminates the return of premiums already paid, as the return-of-premium feature terminates upon conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">TERMINATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy to permanent insurance eliminates the return-of-premium benefit, meaning the financial incentive tied to timely payment is lost upon exercise of the conversion option.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without medical proof does not affect the restriction on policy loans. These provisions operate independently regarding policy benefits and flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance without medical proof does not affect the restriction on partial withdrawals. Both are independent policy provisions governing different types of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy to permanent insurance eliminates the return-of-premium benefit, thereby restricting access to cash value solely to full surrender or maturity. This means the conversion privilege limits future options for receiving funds from the policy's accumulated value.</data>
  <data key="d4">TERMINATES BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The conversion privilege allows the policyholder to transition from a term policy with defined premiums ($1,620 annually) into permanent coverage, effectively altering the financial and structural nature of the original agreement, including loss of the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONVERTS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">The conversion privilege allows policyholders to transition from a temporary term plan to permanent coverage without underwriting, although doing so eliminates the return-of-premium feature tied to regular annual payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy eliminates the right to receive the return of premiums, meaning the ability to convert undermines the fulfillment of the return-of-premium condition outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="5875c040-ac0c-4e62-bbe3-c3cc925fe67d">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the policy was issued on September 15, 2024, helps contextualize the window for exercising the conversion option, ensuring it occurs before the deadline specified in the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without medical proof complements the stability of the ROP payout, which remains intact even if age was inaccurately reported during application.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e75cd5ef-3059-4075-b9ec-962016086fda" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
