<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy before expiration allows for long-term planning options, regardless of the specific premium amount required annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance anytime before expiration depends on maintaining active status through consistent premium payments, such as those due on September 15 annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance anytime before expiration provides flexibility regardless of whether premiums rise or stay level. Premium levels have no bearing on when conversion may occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance before expiration does not affect the timing or completeness of premium payments required for the return-of-premium benefit, nor vice versa.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance before expiration enables long-term planning options regardless of payment history. This provision operates independently of the grace period for premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">The option to convert to permanent insurance exists before expiration regardless of payment status. However, if a premium isn't paid during the grace period, the policy lapses and conversion becomes impossible.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance before expiration provides a strategic option that could prevent lapsing and preserve benefits like return of premiums, especially when financial hardship arises.</data>
  <data key="d4">AVOIDS_FORFEITURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">Conversion privileges allow policyholders to switch to permanent insurance before termination, regardless of past payment issues, meaning delayed or missed premiums do not affect eligibility for conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance anytime before expiration exists regardless of whether premiums were paid late. Late payments impact the return benefit but do not restrict access to conversion privileges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">Being able to convert without medical proof makes it possible to exercise the option at any point before the policy terminates.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy before it expires enables access to permanent coverage under specific conditions, including meeting a minimum conversion amount of $50,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 claims conversion is possible before expiration, but fact_sentence_2 clarifies that it must also happen before age 65, making age 65 a hard cutoff regardless of remaining term length.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes a general timeframe for conversion availability, stating it can occur before policy expiration. Fact_sentence_2 refines this by specifying that conversion is limited to before age 65, adding a stricter temporal constraint.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy before expiration enables access to coverage, while the $300,000 ceiling defines the upper bound of such conversions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy before expiration leads directly to the loss of the return-of-premium benefit upon execution of the conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy at any time before expiration sets the timing condition under which the maximum conversion amount applies. This ensures flexibility in accessing permanent coverage, subject to the cap defined by the current face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">The availability of conversion before policy expiry allows the insured to switch to permanent coverage, but the premium cost for the new policy depends on the individual's age at the moment of conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance does not affect the restriction on policy loans. Both provisions operate independently regarding policyholder benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert before policy expiration leads directly to the loss of refunded premiums already paid. Conversion terminates the return-of-premium feature, meaning past contributions are forfeited upon switching.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance does not affect the restriction against partial withdrawals. Both provisions operate independently regarding policy benefits and flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder converts to permanent insurance before maturity, they forfeit the return-of-premium benefit, limiting future access to cash value solely to surrender with reduced payout based on payment history or waiting until term end.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ca65d2b-1bef-431b-8b5c-d6557547ae91" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">available_before</data>
</edge>
