  <data key="d3">The maximum conversion amount of $300,000 indicates a potential benefit upon converting to permanent insurance, unrelated to the stated annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The maximum conversion amount of $300,000 sets a financial ceiling for converting to permanent insurance, independent of when the annual premium is due.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence specifies a maximum conversion benefit of $300,000 under the conversion privilege. This figure has no bearing on whether premiums remain level, as it pertains solely to benefits available upon conversion rather than payment terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The maximum conversion amount of $300,000 sets a financial ceiling for switching to permanent insurance but has no bearing on whether premiums were paid on time or if the return-of-premium benefit is retained.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 limit on conversion applies regardless of whether a grace period was used for premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">The maximum conversion amount is capped at $300,000 regardless of whether the policy lapsed due to missed premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The maximum conversion amount is capped at $300,000 regardless of whether the return-of-premium benefit was lost due to lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows conversion to permanent insurance up to $300,000, but this option terminates the return-of-premium feature. Whether premiums were missed has no bearing on this cap.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 ceiling on conversion privileges is unrelated to the consequences of paying premiums late or the associated reduction in refund benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without medical proof applies, but only up to a maximum of $300,000 in coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">The $300,000 maximum conversion amount sets a financial limit regardless of when conversion occurs during the policy’s life.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">The maximum conversion amount of $300,000 defines the upper financial limit for the conversion privilege. This cap applies regardless of whether the conversion occurs before age 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">The conversion privilege allows access to permanent insurance with a maximum coverage of $300,000, but this option must be exercised before age 65 or before the policy expires, whichever comes first.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the highest allowable conversion amount, which complements fact_sentence_1's definition of the minimum threshold, forming complete boundaries for the conversion privilege.</data>
  <data key="d4">BOUNDARY_RANGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">The conversion privilege allows switching to permanent insurance up to $300,000, with the resulting premium calculated according to the insured's current age at the time of conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets a hard upper limit on conversion eligibility, while fact_sentence_2 indicates that the actual allowable conversion depends on the policy's current face value. Thus, the maximum conversion is constrained by whichever is lower—the face amount or $300,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">Conversion allows access to permanent insurance up to $300,000, but doing so results in the termination of the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows conversion to permanent insurance up to $300,000, but does not permit policy loans. This highlights distinct limitations on accessing cash value through either conversion or borrowing mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">Conversion allows access to up to $300,000 in permanent insurance without medical underwriting, but any premiums already paid are forfeited upon conversion, eliminating potential returns from earlier contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows conversion to permanent insurance up to $300,000, but does not permit partial withdrawals from the cash value. This describes separate restrictions related to benefit options and fund accessibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">The conversion privilege allows upgrading to permanent insurance up to $300,000, but doing so forfeits the return-of-premium benefit. Access to cash value is restricted to full surrender or maturity, consistent with the loss of return benefits upon conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
