  <data key="d3">Converting the policy eliminates the return-of-premium benefit, which was originally enabled by consistent payment of the $1,620 annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">Exercising the conversion privilege results in loss of the return-of-premium benefit, making it essential to meet all premium deadlines before conversion to retain any potential refund.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy eliminates the return-of-premium feature, meaning the financial incentive tied to consistent payment history—and thus dependent on predictable, level premiums—is lost. Therefore, the decision to convert hinges on accepting the loss of this guaranteed return.</data>
  <data key="d4">TERMINATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy eliminates the return-of-premium benefit, meaning even if all premiums were paid on time, the full refund cannot be received after conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENDS ELIGIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance triggers the termination of the return-of-premium feature, meaning that even if all premiums were paid within the grace period, the benefit would still be lost upon conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES FORFEITURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy to permanent insurance terminates the return-of-premium benefit. This action may occur even if premiums were timely paid, so it operates independently of whether a grace period was violated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy eliminates the return-of-premium feature, just as failing to make timely payments results in its forfeiture, showing parallel pathways to losing the same benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance causes the return-of-premium benefit to be lost, regardless of whether premiums were paid on time. This outcome aligns with the rule that any deviation from standard terms voids the benefit, including termination via conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">TERMINATES BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy to permanent insurance causes immediate forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit. This contrasts with late payments, which only partially reduce the benefit rather than eliminating it completely.</data>
  <data key="d4">TERMINATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit occurs specifically because the policyholder chooses to convert it into permanent insurance, making the outcome contingent on the action described in sentence one.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy before its expiration causes the forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, making such a decision irreversible regarding that feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">Converting to permanent insurance before age 65 causes the forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, making timely conversion contingent on accepting this trade-off.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium benefit is lost if conversion occurs, which is limited to happening before age 65 or before policy expiry, whichever comes first.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of a minimum $50,000 conversion amount specifies one criterion for exercising the conversion privilege, which inherently results in losing the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CONVERSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium benefit is lost when converting to permanent insurance, regardless of the conversion amount, including if it reaches the $300,000 cap.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">The return-of-premium benefit ceases when conversion occurs, so any attempt to convert cannot exceed the existing face amount, ensuring alignment with the policy’s defined limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITION_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit upon conversion directly follows from exercising the conversion privilege, which initiates a new policy whose premium is recalculated based on the insured's current age.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit upon conversion does not affect the availability of policy loans, which remain prohibited regardless of conversion status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">Conversion terminates the return-of-premium benefit, meaning no future refunds are available. This directly implies that even if premiums were paid earlier, they won’t be returned upon conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">Conversion results in loss of the return-of-premium benefit, reinforcing why alternative liquidity options like partial withdrawals are disallowed to preserve policy integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSISTENT_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy results in loss of the return-of-premium benefit, meaning the only remaining avenues to access accumulated cash value are full surrender (subject to penalty reductions) or surviving until the end of the term for full repayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy eliminates the right to receive refunded premiums, meaning the $1,620 annual payments no longer lead to a payout at maturity unless conversion is avoided.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS_BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy nullifies the return-of-premium benefit, despite meeting the annual payment obligation outlined in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS_BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy, as noted in fact_sentence_2, directly eliminates the right to receive the $32,400 return specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="5875c040-ac0c-4e62-bbe3-c3cc925fe67d">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy nullifies the return-of-premium benefit, making the initial issuance date irrelevant once such a change takes place.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance results in forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit, regardless of any age-related inaccuracies in application. This ensures that while age misstatements don’t alter the ROP amount, structural changes like conversion still eliminate the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
