<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy results in the non-refundability of already-paid premiums, meaning any $1,620 annually contributed cannot be recovered after conversion occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy terminates the return-of-premium feature, meaning any premiums already paid cannot be recovered, regardless of whether they were paid on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy to permanent insurance results in the loss of the return-of-premium benefit, meaning earlier stable premiums cannot be recovered—even though they remained constant over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The inability to get refunded premiums after conversion undermines the incentive to maintain timely payments if one plans to convert. Thus, while timely payments ensure the return under normal conditions, they do not protect against loss of benefits during conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy terminates the return-of-premium feature, meaning no refund of past premiums—even those paid before the conversion. This outcome stands independently of whether earlier payments were made within a grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">IRRELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">Conversion terminates the return-of-premium feature and means previous premiums won’t be refunded, regardless of whether earlier payments were timely. This condition stands independently of any lapse caused by late payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The second statement notes that upon conversion, previous premiums are not returned. This complements the first statement, which indicates that missing payments also voids the return benefit, showing multiple pathways to lose access to repaid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">Converting the policy results in loss of refunded premiums, which underscores why missing payments permanently jeopardizes benefits since conversions also eliminate refund eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">TERMINATES BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">Conversion terminates the return-of-premium feature regardless of past payment timeliness, meaning even if all premiums were paid on time, no refunds occur after conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">The inability to receive a refund of past premiums is a direct outcome of exercising the conversion privilege to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums paid to date are not returned after conversion, it implies that such conversions must occur within the window when they're permitted—before the policy's expiration—to maintain eligibility under the terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">If premiums were paid under the return-of-premium policy, they cannot be recovered once the policyholder converts to permanent insurance, even if done before age 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">The inability to recover previous premiums after conversion depends on meeting the deadline defined by the earlier of age 65 or policy expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">Once a policyholder converts to permanent insurance, they lose the right to receive back premiums paid so far, regardless of whether the conversion met the $50,000 minimum requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF_CONVERSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums paid before conversion are not refunded, even if the conversion reaches its maximum allowable amount ($300,000), the policyholder loses those accumulated payments regardless of the new coverage size.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Although premiums paid to date are not refunded upon conversion, the resulting policy’s face amount cannot exceed the original policy’s current face amount, limiting how much protection one can obtain through the conversion privilege.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT OF LIMIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">Since converted policies begin anew with updated pricing based on attained age, any premiums already paid before conversion are not returned, aligning with the principle that old benefits cease when switching plans.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums paid to date aren't returned upon conversion, it follows that the return-of-premium feature—which would have refunded those amounts—is also lost.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">Conversion results in loss of refundable premiums, but this does not affect loan availability. Policy loans remain prohibited regardless of conversion status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Conversion eliminates the possibility of returning past premiums, reinforcing that the only viable paths to recover cash value are full surrender (subject to penalty) or surviving until maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance terminates the return-of-premium benefit, meaning earlier premiums are forfeited. This restriction aligns with the broader rule prohibiting partial withdrawals, reinforcing the policy's lack of interim access to cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6e44ae9-c0e4-4c51-8580-81db03a7c89d" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">not refunded upon conversion</data>
</edge>
<edge source="98db3f0f-eb08-4c34-9724-111641f21327" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">not refunded upon conversion</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d34ad7-ca01-4e85-98bd-ccd7abb345f9" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">does not result in refund of premiums</data>
</edge>
<edge source="32278384-aaa1-47d5-b8aa-2410b94e4500" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is result of</data>
</edge>
<edge source="152a6098-b29b-4b10-a1cc-4d66406ccab3" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">not refunded upon conversion</data>
</edge>
