  <data key="d4">CONDITION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="03359885-6e99-47c0-961c-82890d7c09c8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AGE_THRESHOLD</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="cbad65bc-8473-4745-86cd-73161b886a07">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT_RANGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="0385a88d-2c9a-40fc-951c-b3d4a27f09da">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT_RANGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="5798388b-fd8a-4fcc-b3e6-b65543a54d9f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="52d687a6-029c-4181-8e35-6c8a2ac41e1a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="af2b312c-85fd-4615-a5a3-bf54c70003ad">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">NON_REFUNDABLE_COST</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="d40b2ded-46d0-4ec1-b4e8-a148ea839298">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="2fd3daf2-ce48-4f35-b120-d606e17ca2b7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="d89520c4-dc29-4e4e-89ac-3a15dab7ba15">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CASH_ACCESS_METHOD</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="f0c0200a-ef05-4355-bdda-7043a027c20f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CASH_ACCESS_METHOD</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">The absence of policy loan availability reflects a restriction on liquidity, independent of the set annual premium amount required for the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of policy loans has no bearing on when the annual premium is due. This limitation stands independently from the payment schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The absence of policy loan options reflects a restriction on liquidity, whereas fixed premiums ensure predictable cost over time. Neither condition influences nor depends upon the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on policy loans limits how cash value may be used, but does not affect the criteria for qualifying for the return-of-premium benefit based on timely payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Prohibiting policy loans limits how policyholders can access funds during the term, whereas the grace period provides temporary relief from penalty if a premium is paid late. Both features reflect constraints on financial maneuverability but operate through distinct mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of policy loans is unrelated to whether premiums are paid on time or lapsed, as it is a separate structural limitation of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The second statement notes that policy loans are prohibited, meaning cash value cannot be borrowed against. This restriction stands independently from the condition that lapse due to unpaid premiums results in forfeiture of benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of policy loans means borrowers cannot access cash value during the term. This limitation does not affect the rules around missed premiums, which remain governed solely by payment timeliness.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition of policy loans has no bearing on how late payments affect the return-of-premium benefit, as they pertain to separate policy features.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of policy loans is unrelated to the option to convert to permanent insurance without medical proof, as neither condition influences the other’s existence or application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on policy loans has no bearing on the timing or eligibility of converting the policy to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against policy loans has no bearing on the timing or eligibility of converting to permanent insurance before age 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on policy loans applies universally across the policy’s duration. It has no bearing on the timing constraints for conversion to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">The absence of policy loans means cash value cannot be borrowed against, which operates independently from the condition requiring a $50,000 minimum for conversion to permanent coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">While policy loans are unavailable, the policy permits conversion to permanent insurance with a cap of $300,000. Both restrictions relate to how benefits may be accessed during the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Since policy loans are not permitted under this policy, it has no bearing on the upper limit of the conversion privilege, which depends solely on the existing face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on policy loans applies universally across all phases of the policy lifecycle, including after conversion to permanent insurance, where premiums are recalculated based on attained age.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on policy loans has no bearing on whether the return-of-premium benefit is retained after conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on policy loans applies universally, even if the policyholder converts it, whereupon premiums paid are forfeited.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition of policy loans complements the restriction on partial withdrawals, together limiting how policyholders may access accumulated cash value during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Since policy loans are prohibited, the only viable avenues for accessing cash value are full surrender (with reduced returns if premiums were delayed) or waiting until the end of the term for full repayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of policy loans complements the high premium burden ($1,620 annually), emphasizing that borrowers cannot use the policy as a credit source despite paying substantial amounts over 20 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of policy loans supports the necessity of regular annual payments, ensuring funds remain locked into the policy to maintain eligibility for the return-of-premium payout at maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">The inability to take policy loans aligns with the structure requiring full premium payment discipline to secure the $32,400 return, emphasizing long-term commitment over interim liquidity options.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="5875c040-ac0c-4e62-bbe3-c3cc925fe67d">
  <data key="d3">The absence of policy loans underscores why the return-of-premium feature depends solely on timely payment rather than flexible financial options during the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES_RESTRICTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of policy loans relates to the policy’s design constraints, whereas the stability of the ROP amount despite age misstatements reflects its non-taxable, fixed-return nature. Both highlight structural safeguards within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7e772258-12f4-4840-beb1-ea992c103a46" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
