<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">The restriction against partial withdrawals aligns with the broader design of the policy, where access to funds is limited to full surrender or maturity, consistent with maintaining defined premium and payout conditions such as the $1,620 annual requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against partial withdrawals means policyholders cannot access funds early, regardless of timely premium payments. This rule operates separately from the due date of the annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">Restrictions on partial withdrawals limit liquidity options, whereas fixed premiums ensure predictable cost over time. Neither condition affects the validity or outcome of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">Prohibiting partial withdrawals means policyholders cannot access funds early, whereas timely premium payments are necessary to secure the full return at maturity. Neither rule directly affects the enforcement or meaning of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Prohibiting partial withdrawals limits liquidity options for policyholders, but this rule operates independently of the grace period offered for premium payments, which concerns timeliness rather than fund usage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against partial withdrawals means policyholders cannot access funds before termination. This restriction operates regardless of whether premiums were paid on time or not.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on partial withdrawals means cash value cannot be accessed early, independent of whether premiums were paid on time or if the return-of-premium benefit was lost.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">The inability to make partial withdrawals means policyholders cannot tap into accumulated cash value before termination. This rule stands separately from the non-recovery of missed premiums, which concerns payment timing rather than fund access.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on partial withdrawals means policyholders cannot access funds early, independent of whether premiums were paid on time or late.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">Restrictions on partial withdrawals do not influence the availability of the conversion privilege to permanent insurance without medical proof. Each rule operates independently within the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">Restrictions on partial withdrawals do not influence the timing or eligibility for converting the policy into permanent coverage. Each rule applies separately to distinct policy functions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">Restrictions on partial withdrawals do not influence the timing or eligibility for converting to permanent insurance. Each rule applies independently to different aspects of policy usage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence prohibits partial withdrawals from the policy’s cash value. This rule stands independently of the timeline constraints governing conversion privileges mentioned in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">While the policy restricts partial withdrawals, it permits conversion to permanent insurance with a minimum coverage of $50,000, subject to certain conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">While partial withdrawals are disallowed, the policy permits converting to permanent insurance with a cap of $300,000. These features represent distinct limitations on accessing funds or changing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals are disallowed, any attempt to access cash value must occur through full surrender or waiting until maturity, regardless of the conversion privilege tied to the face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">The inability to make partial withdrawals limits flexibility in accessing funds, independent of how premiums are determined when converting to permanent coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on partial withdrawals aligns with the policy’s design where cash value access occurs only through full surrender or maturity, consistent with the termination of benefits upon conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSISTENT_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">Restrictions on partial withdrawals reinforce the absence of policy loan options, emphasizing the overall inflexibility in accessing cash value before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are not allowed, meaning policyholders cannot access funds incrementally. Instead, they must either fully surrender the policy or wait until maturity to receive any cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on partial withdrawals ensures that policyholders cannot access cash value before termination. This limitation complements the rule that converted policies do not return past premiums, emphasizing restricted financial flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The restriction against partial withdrawals complements the requirement to pay $1,620 annually by ensuring that even if premiums are paid, policyholders cannot extract any portion of the money earlier than the end of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on partial withdrawals underscores the importance of maintaining regular annual payments, as any deviation could jeopardize the return-of-premium benefit, making timely annual payments essential for maximizing policy value.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">The promise of a $32,400 return depends on maintaining the policy without early access, making the absence of partial withdrawal options essential to preserving eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="5875c040-ac0c-4e62-bbe3-c3cc925fe67d">
  <data key="d3">The restriction against partial withdrawals, detailed in chunk_summary_2, applies from the moment the policy is issued on September 15, 2024, making the timing consistent with the policy’s operational rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">While partial withdrawals are disallowed under the policy, the ROP amount remains intact regardless of any inaccuracies in reported age during application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
