</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="7fa3f73b-8826-46ec-b4b0-ce2bf73a452d">
  <data key="d3">The restriction that cash value may only be accessed via full surrender or maturity depends on timely premium payments, such as the required $1,620 annual payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="86e64861-deab-4ac4-a343-0965992b4344">
  <data key="d3">Accessing cash value via full surrender or maturity depends on maintaining timely premium payments, which preserve the return-of-premium benefit outlined in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON_PAYMENT_HISTORY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="cb413827-b3ae-48d1-91af-f9043f9af205">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on accessing cash value unless premiums are paid on time relies on the premise that premiums do not change over time, ensuring predictable qualification criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The ability to receive the full return of premium at maturity depends entirely on making all payments on time, meaning timely payment is required to unlock the final payout option mentioned in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="aacfe1a1-50cb-4a0f-b92f-585491bb31a4">
  <data key="d3">Accessing cash value depends on meeting conditions like timely payments, so any use of the grace period could jeopardize future benefits outlined in fact_sentence_2 regarding return percentages.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="16950aa2-96cc-49d7-82e7-9c271feae822">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on accessing cash value unless the policy survives to surrender or maturity means that if a premium is missed during the grace period, the policy lapsed, making the methods outlined in fact_sentence_2 unattainable.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS ON SURVIVAL TO MATURITY OR SURRENDER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">The restriction that only full surrender or end-of-term payout allows access to cash value implies that failing to pay premiums leads to lapse, thereby triggering forfeiture of the return-of-premium benefit described in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_CONSEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="f9289efc-c4d1-43b2-b195-d430210c3e20">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on accessing cash value except through full surrender or term-end payout depends critically on maintaining timely premium payments; since missed premiums cannot be corrected, such outcomes become unattainable if payments lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON PAYMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The restriction that cash value can only be accessed via surrender or maturity means that any reduction in the return due to late payments directly affects the actual amount received upon withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="790d6283-257a-4b49-ba90-001cca666300">
  <data key="d3">Accessing cash value exclusively through surrender or maturity implies that any decision to convert the policy would forfeit those payout opportunities, making the conversion privilege contingent upon giving up guaranteed return benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="b2fca366-b20a-44a1-90b5-1fd965a9c28c">
  <data key="d3">Accessing cash value through surrender or maturity depends on whether the return-of-premium feature was maintained, which is contingent upon not exercising the conversion option prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="4f1b8053-abbc-4db1-bef3-444bf9ee8a3b">
  <data key="d3">Access to cash value is limited to full surrender or maturity, whereas conversion eligibility extends before age 65. Neither provision directly influences nor depends on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="8137a6da-6508-4c6a-972b-8593add581bd">
  <data key="d3">Cash value may only be accessed via full surrender or waiting until term end. This limitation has no bearing on the deadline for converting to permanent insurance, which depends solely on age or expiration date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="47677240-df4c-430b-8559-b97fbc6bd329">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes limited avenues for accessing cash value—either through full surrender or waiting until maturity. This restriction indirectly affects the practical utility of the conversion privilege mentioned in fact_sentence_1, particularly if one intends to use converted coverage as part of a liquidity strategy.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="0f394164-4990-4d22-9ccc-0de82ecc6299">
  <data key="d3">Cash value may only be accessed via full surrender or maturity, conditions tied to the retention of return-of-premium eligibility. This restriction implies that converting under the $300,000 cap ends such eligibility, limiting future access options.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="d48c4b09-f755-40f7-86b5-87f5374d83de">
  <data key="d3">Cash value can only be accessed via surrender or maturity, regardless of whether the policyholder exercises the conversion option. Conversion privileges do not alter withdrawal rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="8c100aa7-42e6-46f4-9012-c65d6466d8cb">
  <data key="d3">Cash value can only be accessed via surrender or maturity, independent of whether the policy was converted. Conversion affects future premiums but not withdrawal mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="ab97e8fc-5b0b-4cdc-8c51-20501dcc87d7">
  <data key="d3">The inability to access cash value except through full surrender or maturity implies that any action terminating the return-of-premium feature—such as conversion—results in irreversible forfeiture of that benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">TERMINATES ACCESS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="1233ae69-913e-4cbe-8257-e9ce2d717e4f">
  <data key="d3">The restriction against policy loans aligns with the limitation that cash value may only be accessed through full surrender or maturity, confirming that alternative withdrawal mechanisms are excluded.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="fdb3964a-1dd5-48be-85ed-7f975e84c191">
  <data key="d3">Since converted policies do not allow return of premiums paid, the sole remaining avenues for accessing accumulated value are full surrender or waiting until the end of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="99b3ae6a-0f70-4f20-a89c-8b78a2e28a24">
  <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals are disallowed, the only viable options for accessing cash value are full surrender or surviving until the end of the term when the full return of premium applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The terms governing access to returned premiums—only via full surrender or term completion—are dependent on consistently paying the $1,620 annual premium, reinforcing its central role in the policy’s financial mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on accessing cash value unless premiums are fully paid annually, as stated in fact_sentence_2, directly relies on the annual premium model established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the exclusive methods for accessing cash value, including returning premiums at term's end, which directly enables the scenario detailed in fact_sentence_1 about receiving $32,400 when the policy matures successfully.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="5875c040-ac0c-4e62-bbe3-c3cc925fe67d">
  <data key="d3">The condition that the full return of premiums is available only upon surviving the term and making all payments on time relies on the policy’s effective start date, specified in fact_sentence_1, to determine eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes procedural constraints on accessing ROP benefits, while fact_sentence_2 clarifies that these benefits are immune to changes caused by inaccurate age reporting, ensuring predictability in the payout despite underwriting issues.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that cash value may only be accessed via full surrender with ROP deduction or waiting until term end. Fact sentence 2 repeats this exact mechanism, confirming consistency across both chunks regarding withdrawal options.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make timely premiums may lead to loss of return-of-premium benefits, potentially necessitating policy reinstatement later under stricter terms involving interest charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">Accessing cash value depends on maintaining continuous premium payments; failing to do so risks losing benefits and necessitating reinstatement later, which involves proving insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">Accessing cash value depends on uninterrupted premium payments and surviving the term; reinstatement after lapse preserves eligibility under certain conditions, ensuring continuation toward eventual ROP qualification despite past lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, the return-of-premium benefit may be forfeited, but reinstatement within five years restores eligibility—though it resets the ROP clock and restarts contestability. This contrasts with fact_sentence_1’s assertion that timely payments are required to preserve the full return.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy after a lapse adjusts the return-of-premium benefit by removing the impact of the inactive period, meaning the original terms for receiving full ROP may still apply once reinstated, but only from the point of revival onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement may affect the ability to receive a full return of premiums under fact_sentence_1, as it resets the ROP calculation and could invalidate previous compliance with payment schedules. Additionally, the new contestability period introduced in fact_sentence_2 adds risk during reinstitution phase.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the limited mechanisms for accessing cash value tied to the return-of-premium feature, while fact_sentence_2 attributes the policy's higher price precisely to that same feature, explaining why such restrictions exist financially.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_REASON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
