<edge source="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">The ROP policy's design includes a suicide exclusion within the initial two-year period, aligning with standard industry practices and ensuring that the promise of returning premiums does not extend to cases involving intentional self-harm early in the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_COVERAGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause limits the payment of the death benefit even if the insured dies during the 20-year term, specifically disqualifying claims made within the first two years after policy issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_LIMITATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">While the policy refunds all premiums if the insured lives past the 20-year term, it explicitly denies payouts for suicides within the initial two-year period—even if the individual had been paying premiums consistently toward eventual return eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_SURVIVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies by suicide within 24 months, no death benefit is paid—even though the policy has accumulated $32,400 in premiums, which would otherwise be fully refunded upon survival.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON_PREMIUMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">While the second fact limits death benefit payments in cases of suicide within two years, it does not affect the return of premiums upon survival after the 20-year term, meaning the outcome described in the first fact remains unaffected regardless of the suicide clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
