<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">A two-year contestability clause allows insurers to challenge claims due to misrepresentation, regardless of whether the policyholder chooses to surrender the policy early or wait for full ROP at term end.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="b9a34ec6-add4-44c5-a78e-96dfa4d2ce04">
  <data key="d3">Material misrepresentation allows the insurer to void coverage during the first two years, potentially affecting any benefit—including those related to suicide—but does not alter the specific terms around suicide payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202">
  <data key="d3">Insurers have the right to contest policies within two years of issue when material misrepresentations were made. One such scenario leading to denial of benefits is suicide occurring within the first two years, reinforcing the purpose of the contestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns the insurer's right to challenge claims due to false information during underwriting. This does not relate to whether war-related deaths are excluded from coverage, which is addressed separately in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns the insurer's right to challenge claims due to false information during underwriting. This does not influence whether aviation-related risks are excluded from coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="b4003548-05a1-4f13-a791-01db074853b9">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns the insurer's right to challenge claims due to false information during underwriting. This does not influence or relate to whether travel-related risks are excluded from coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns the insurer's right to challenge claims due to false information during underwriting. This does not influence or relate to whether hazardous activities are excluded from coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause applies during the first two years regardless of lapses, but it does not affect reinstatement rights. Reinstatement depends on meeting specific criteria like proof of insurability and premium payment, independent of prior misrepresentations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the insurer’s right to challenge claims during the early contestability period due to misrepresentation. This does not affect the second sentence, which describes conditions required to restore coverage after a lapse, including proving current insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the insurer's right to challenge claims due to false information in applications within the initial two years. This does not directly influence the second sentence, which specifies the monetary obligations required to restore coverage after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The initial contestability clause applies at issuance, but when a policy is reinstated after lapse, it restarts the same type of review period, creating a renewed window during which claims can be contested.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESETS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines a condition affecting claim validity due to application accuracy, whereas the second describes a financial characteristic tied to the policy’s design. They operate independently within the same context but do not influence each other logically.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">The contestability period applies when the policy is initially issued, ensuring claims aren't paid if misrepresentations were made early on. This does not affect the recalculation of ROP upon reinstatement, which depends solely on the renewed active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause applies early in the policy lifecycle, potentially invalidating benefits if misrepresentation occurred. This does not affect reinstatement unless the insured's survival status becomes contested later.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">If the insured survives the 20-year term without any contested issues, the policy guarantees a full return of premiums, but only if the initial application did not contain material misrepresentations subject to contestability.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability clause restricts the insurer’s right to dispute claims during the beginning of the 20-year term, making the timing of the insured’s passing crucial for determining eligibility for benefit payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
