  <data key="d3">The possibility of reinstating a lapsed policy within five years requires meeting certain financial obligations, such as repaying overdue premiums with 6% annual interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy initiates a fresh two-year contestability and suicide exclusion period, ensuring updated underwriting scrutiny applies from the date of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy within five years depends on the insured surviving past the lapse period. Without ongoing life, reinstatement cannot occur regardless of other conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility within five years enables the policyholder to restore coverage, leading to a recalculation of the Return-of-Premium benefit that disregards the inactive period during the lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 discusses the timeframe for reinstating a lapsed policy, focusing on conditions like proof of insurability and payment terms. Fact sentence 2 explains that the policy's higher cost stems from the return-of-premium benefit, unrelated to reinstatement rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
