  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy ensures continuation of coverage needed to qualify for the return of premiums at the end of the term, thus supporting the fulfillment of the financial benefit described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility within five years after a lapse implies that the original 20-year term remains intact upon restoration, meaning the policy's long-term structure—including eventual return of premiums—is preserved despite temporary interruption.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a lapse interrupts the continuity required for full ROP eligibility, potentially invalidating the condition that requires uninterrupted payment throughout the entire 20-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS_IF_LAPSED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
