  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy invalidates the path to receiving the $32,400 return-of-premium payment because continuity of coverage is broken.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2">
  <data key="d3">While the policy has a 20-year term, the ability to reinstate it within 5 years after a lapse means that surviving beyond this period without lapses ensures eligibility for the return of premiums, making the reinstatement clause relevant to fulfilling the long-term benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy after lapse depends on actions taken prior to the final expiration date of September 15, 2044, making the end date a critical temporal boundary for exercising this option.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
