  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restores active status but nullifies previous progress toward the return-of-premium benefit, meaning future eligibility depends on meeting all conditions anew from the point of reinstatement onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy enables future compliance, but any past late payments already triggered a 10% reduction in the return-of-premium benefit, which cannot be reversed upon revival.</data>
  <data key="d4">PARTIALLY_DEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a lapse cannot reverse the forfeiture of the return of premium benefit, making the recovery of that financial advantage impossible even if coverage is restored.</data>
  <data key="d4">DOES_NOT_RESTORE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
