<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes a prerequisite for reinstating a lapsed policy, whereas fact_sentence_1 explains how cash value may be obtained under normal circumstances. These statements concern different procedural phases and do not directly influence each other’s validity or outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="b9a34ec6-add4-44c5-a78e-96dfa4d2ce04">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires proof of insurability but has no bearing on whether a claim would be denied due to suicide during the initial two-year period. The two rules operate independently within different contexts.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires providing proof of insurability, independent of whether suicide occurred within the contestability period. The requirement for evidence of insurability applies regardless of prior claims or exclusions like suicide.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires demonstrating insurability, independent of whether prior misrepresentations were made. While such past issues could impact eligibility, the requirement itself is unrelated to the timing of contestability from the original issue date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires proving insurability, ensuring the individual remains eligible despite prior lapses. This condition stands separately from whether certain risks like war are excluded from coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">Requiring proof of insurability for reinstatement applies regardless of whether aviation is excluded, meaning this condition stands independently of exclusion policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="b4003548-05a1-4f13-a791-01db074853b9">
  <data key="d3">Requiring proof of insurability for reinstatement ensures the insurer assesses current risk before restoring coverage. This condition stands independently of whether travel exclusions exist.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">Requiring proof of insurability during reinstatement ensures ongoing risk assessment, independent of whether hazardous activities were previously excluded from coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">Providing satisfactory evidence of insurability is necessary to qualify for reinstating a lapsed policy within the allowed five-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required to reinstate a lapsed policy, but such verification is only meaningful if the individual remains alive at the time of application.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of insurability allows the policyholder to reinstate coverage, after which a fresh two-year contestability and suicide exclusion period commences.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of insurability allows the policyholder to reinstate coverage, triggering a reset of the Return-of-Premium (ROP) calculation that excludes the inactive period during lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that proof of insurability is mandatory before reinstatement. This condition supports the need for fact sentence 2’s stipulation regarding premium payments, ensuring the insurer assesses risk prior to accepting financial commitments.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to prove insurability upon reinstatement does not relate to the increased cost of the policy driven by the return-of-premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">While the second fact focuses on reinstating a lapsed ROP policy, it relies on underlying assumptions about the original policy’s nature—such as having a defined term and underwriting process—which aligns with the characteristics detailed in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement requires proof of insurability within five years of lapse, meaning that even though the policy lasts 20 years, any interruption could limit future options unless acted upon promptly.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORAL_CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires proof of insurability, which could affect whether future returns are available. However, since the return of premiums depends solely on continuous payment and survival through the entire term, reinstatement does not alter that outcome unless it occurs before the original term ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires meeting specific criteria including proof of insurability, which ensures ongoing eligibility for benefits like the return of premiums originally outlined in the initial agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires demonstrating insurability, which could affect whether future premium refunds like those described in fact_sentence_1 remain accessible. However, the refund itself depends solely on continuous payment and survival through the original term, regardless of lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires proving insurability, which could affect whether the original terms—including the eventual return of $32,400—are still attainable upon reaching the final term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2">
  <data key="d3">Requiring proof of insurability upon reinstatement implies that surviving beyond the initial term without lapses ensures eligibility for benefits, reinforcing the importance of maintaining coverage throughout the full 20-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement requires proof of insurability, but only applies prior to the policy's end date on September 15, 2044, meaning the timeframe limits when such action can be taken.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability upon reinstatement implies that failure to maintain payments could lead to lapsation, making it essential to meet the original premium obligation of $1,620 annually to avoid triggering these restoration conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">Requiring proof of insurability to reinstate a lapsed policy implies ongoing risk assessment, which contextualizes why consistent annual payments are critical—failure to pay may trigger reinstatement requirements unrelated to initial eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires demonstrating insurability, which becomes necessary because failing to pay premiums on time voids the return-of-premium benefit as outlined in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy after a late payment may restore coverage, but it does not reverse the penalty applied to the return-of-premium benefit from the original delay.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires proving insurability, which may prevent reactivation of the original return-of-premium benefit unless terms are fully satisfied during reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restores eligibility for future returns of premium but does not restore past lost benefits related to earlier non-payment, thus affecting long-term access to cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
