  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying delinquent premiums with 6% interest, whereas the first statement explains that suicide within two years results in limited payout. Both relate to financial consequences but apply to separate events and outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42" target="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202">
  <data key="d3">Repayment of overdue premiums with 6% interest is required to reinstate a lapsed policy but has no bearing on whether a suicide death claim would be paid during the initial two-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42" target="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that reinstating a lapsed policy requires payment of overdue premiums plus 6% interest. This condition stands independently from the contestability clause tied to misrepresentation in the original application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
