  <data key="d3">Paying overdue premiums with 6% interest is required to reinstate a lapsed policy, but this step cannot occur unless the insured is still alive.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">Paying overdue premiums with 6% interest enables reinstatement, which in turn initiates a fresh two-year contestability and suicide exclusion period.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">Paying overdue premiums with 6% interest allows reinstatement, which leads to the recalculation of the Return of Premium (ROP) benefit, now excluding the inactive lapse period.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes the financial conditions required to reinstate a lapsed policy, specifically involving repayment of overdue premiums with interest. This detail is unrelated to why the policy has a higher cost than standard term life insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed ROP policy involves repaying delinquent payments with interest, which impacts whether the full premium return is ultimately realized, directly tying into the policy’s core financial promise.</data>
