  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy involves paying back unpaid premiums with interest, which contrasts with the scenario described in fact_sentence_1 where all premiums were timely paid, ensuring eligibility for the full refund without additional charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 provides rules for restoring a failed policy, which could prevent the scenario described in fact_sentence_1 where the policyholder receives a refund. Thus, failing to meet reinstatement terms may disqualify someone from qualifying for the return of premiums.</data>
