  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy involves repaying past-due premiums with interest, whereas failing to pay on time during the grace period triggers a 10% reduction in the return of premium benefit. These rules govern distinct phases of payment delinquency—one preventive (grace period), one corrective (post-lapse).</data>
