</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Survival of the insured enables reinstatement of the policy, which may allow continuation toward qualifying for the full return of premiums, assuming all payments are eventually made over the extended period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">Survival beyond the 20-year term enables the return of $32,400, but only if the policy was not previously lapsed and successfully reinstated—if applicable—which depends on ongoing survival up to that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">For the return of premium ($32,400) to occur, the policy must remain intact throughout the 20-year term. But if a lapse occurs, reinstatement under fact_sentence_2 requires ongoing survival, making continuation of coverage dependent on maintaining health status over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2">
  <data key="d3">Survival of the insured is necessary for reinstating the policy, ensuring that the original 20-year term framework remains viable upon revival.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">Survival beyond the lapse period but before September 15, 2044, enables reinstatement, thereby affecting whether the policy’s terms—including the final payout—are fulfilled.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy requires surviving past any lapse period, meaning ongoing life expectancy affects the ability to recover coverage—and therefore impacts the necessity of continuing payments like the $1,620 annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">Survival of the insured is a prerequisite for reinstating the policy, making it essential that payments like the annual premium continue uninterrupted to avoid lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to maintain timely premium payments ensures eligibility for the full return of premiums. If lapses occur, reinstatement becomes necessary—but it's contingent upon the insured’s survival, meaning death during the grace period would forfeit any chance of restoring coverage or returning premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">The condition that reinstatement requires the insured's survival ensures that even if a late payment leads to lapse, future restoration of benefits hinges on ongoing life status—not just timely action.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">While reinstatement is permitted if the insured survives past the lapse, doing so does not restore the lost return of premium benefit, making the initial lapse irreversible regarding that specific perk.</data>
  <data key="d4">FORFEITS_IF_LAPSED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy allows recovery of the right to receive full return of premiums at maturity, thereby restoring one of the two pathways mentioned in fact_sentence_1 for accessing cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_ACCESS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
