<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">When a policy is reinstated, the ROP benefit is recalculated without including the lapsed period, aligning with the condition stated in fact_sentence_1 that ROP is available either at surrender or at maturity. Thus, reinstatement preserves eligibility for full ROP, consistent with the core method outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="b9a34ec6-add4-44c5-a78e-96dfa4d2ce04">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement allows the policy to resume with a refreshed ROP calculation that excludes the lapsed period. This procedural detail has no bearing on the conditions surrounding suicide-related claims during the initial contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that upon reinstatement, the ROP calculation excludes the lapsed time. This procedural detail about benefit recalculation has no bearing on the rule that no death benefit is paid for suicide within two years of issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f">
  <data key="d3">When a policy is reinstated, the ROP benefit is recalculated without including the lapsed period, resetting the timeline. This change has no bearing on whether prior misrepresentations could trigger contestability during the original two-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">When a policy is reinstated, the ROP benefit is reset and excludes the lapsed time, ensuring fair recalibration of returns. This process is independent of whether war-related deaths are excluded from coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy triggers a reset of the ROP calculation, removing the lapsed period from consideration, independent of whether aviation risks were excluded.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="b4003548-05a1-4f13-a791-01db074853b9">
  <data key="d3">When a policy is reinstated, the ROP benefit is reset to exclude the lapsed time, ensuring fair recalibration of returns. This adjustment operates independently of whether travel-related exclusions exist.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy triggers a reset of the ROP calculation, removing the impact of the lapsed period. This change does not depend on whether hazardous activities are excluded from coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of the lapsed period from the ROP calculation depends on the successful reinstatement of the policy within the specified five-year timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of the lapsed period from the ROP calculation only occurs after the insurer confirms the applicant’s insurability, making it contingent upon satisfying prior conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">A revised ROP calculation after reinstatement assumes the insured was alive at the time of reinstatement, confirming the necessity of survival for such benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">The resetting of the ROP calculation after reinstatement implies that the prior lapsed period is disregarded, making it necessary to fulfill conditions like paying delinquent premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes how the ROP benefit is adjusted after reinstatement by excluding the lapsed period. This detail relates specifically to policy restoration conditions but does not explain or depend on the pricing rationale behind the policy’s higher cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
  <data key="d3">The recalculation of the ROP benefit excludes the lapsed period, ensuring fair treatment under the return-of-premium feature. This change coincides with the start of a new two-year contestability period, reinforcing regulatory safeguards against fraud after reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">COINCIDES_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy alters the original ROP terms by resetting the calculation to omit the lapsed duration, thereby changing the expected return of premiums outlined in the initial policy description.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">Since the ROP benefit adjusts after reinstatement by removing the lapsed period from consideration, the original 20-year term serves as the reference point for determining how much of the refundable amount remains eligible under revised terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy excludes prior payment periods from the ROP calculation, meaning the initial promise of full premium return may not apply unless the entire term is maintained without interruption.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement excludes the lapsed period from the ROP calculation, so even though $32,400 was originally paid, the actual return depends on whether the policy remained active throughout the term or required reinstatement after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">A successful reinstatement invalidates part of the original ROP eligibility timeline, meaning the full $32,400 return may not apply even if the initial 20-year term was ultimately survived.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON_LAPSE_RECOVERY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces a limitation on the fulfillment of the condition stated in fact_sentence_1: if the policy lapses and is later reinstated, the original $32,400 return cannot be guaranteed because the lapsed period is excluded from the ROP computation.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2">
  <data key="d3">A 20-year term ensures eligibility for the full return-of-premium benefit only if the policy stays active; any lapse triggers a recalculation that excludes the inactive period, potentially diminishing the final refund despite the initial term length.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_TERM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy excludes the lapsed period from the ROP calculation, meaning the final payout depends on whether the policy remains active up to the original end date of September 15, 2044, without interruption beyond the allowed grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">When a policy is reinstated, the exclusion of the lapsed period from the ROP calculation affects the total refundable amount, meaning the initial premium figure of $1,620 per year becomes part of a revised accumulation timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains how the ROP benefit adjusts when a policy is reinstated after lapse, implying that the original annual payment pattern remains applicable once coverage resumes, reinforcing the significance of the annual premium structure mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy invalidates previous ROP accruals, meaning even if the policy was close to full return status, it restarts counting from zero after reinstatement, directly affecting future surrender outcomes described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy resets the ROP accrual timeline, meaning the initial restriction on refunds in years 1–5 could apply anew, regardless of prior coverage duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESETS_TIMELINE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement excludes the lapsed period from the ROP calculation, which directly affects how much of the premiums paid before lapse qualify for return under the schedule outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement excludes the lapsed period from the ROP calculation, which means any progress made toward the 90% return in years 16–19 may be lost if the policy was previously inactive.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder surrenders during Years 11–15 after a lapse and subsequent reinstatement, the ROP benefit may be reduced because the reinvestment timeline restarts, making it harder to reach favorable refund rates despite having lived past Year 15 overall.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">The rule that 100% of premiums are returned after 20 years only applies when the policy remains active continuously; any lapse interrupts this timeline and requires restarting the count from reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The condition for receiving the full return of premiums depends on continuous on-time payments, but reinstating a lapsed policy adjusts the ROP calculation to omit the gap, allowing partial restoration of benefits even after failure to pay.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy resets the ROP calculation to omit the lapsed timeframe, mitigating the negative effect of past late payments on the final return amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">REMEDIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restores eligibility for the return of premium benefit by resetting the calculation to omit the lapsed duration, effectively reversing the forfeiture condition stated in the original fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESTORES_ELIGIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder fails to pay premiums and allows the policy to lapse, they lose the right to receive the full return of premiums unless they reinstate it under specific conditions—including having the ROP benefit recalculated without including the lapsed duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
