<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="6e225e7e-3f3a-47fa-81d2-fc2a41f25361">
  <data key="d3">Upon reinstatement, a new two-year contestability window restarts, affecting eligibility for claims including those involving death from suicide, which indirectly influences whether future cash value access remains viable without challenge.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS_RESET</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="b9a34ec6-add4-44c5-a78e-96dfa4d2ce04">
  <data key="d3">Upon reinstatement, a new two-year suicide and contestability period starts, meaning the earlier restriction under fact_sentence_1 does not apply retroactively if death occurs later during this renewed window.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="b5736d7a-37c0-4f1a-8fc9-f872a4494202">
  <data key="d3">Upon reinstatement, a new two-year suicide exclusion period begins, reinforcing the original rule established at issuance about early-term suicide claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXTENDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="ea5bc4dd-d91e-4ff2-90de-0cc747100f5f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy reinitiates the two-year contestability period, effectively resetting the timeline established at original issuance under conditions like material misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="fb5287ce-2a2a-4ab9-aaea-67aab70121e0">
  <data key="d3">Upon reinstatement, a fresh two-year contestability window begins, ensuring renewed scrutiny of claims. This does not affect the presence or absence of war-related exclusions, which remain permanently absent per policy design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="75bca4d7-1be0-4be8-b8fb-1cf86a7af494">
  <data key="d3">Upon reinstatement, a fresh two-year suicide and contestability period commences regardless of prior history. This rule operates independently of whether aviation is excluded or not, so it has no bearing on the presence or absence of such exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="b4003548-05a1-4f13-a791-01db074853b9">
  <data key="d3">Upon reinstatement, a new two-year suicide and contestability period begins, independent of prior policy history. This condition has no bearing on whether travel-related risks are excluded from coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="71fd7901-e2e8-4c64-a67d-555c1e72b157">
  <data key="d3">Upon reinstatement, a fresh two-year contestability window begins, independent of prior coverage history; meanwhile, the lack of hazardous activity exclusions ensures broader risk acceptance regardless of occupation or behavior.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="3cb7f968-8a8c-43f6-8023-1df17e94f6da">
  <data key="d3">The start of a new two-year suicide and contestability period depends on successfully reinstating the policy within the allowable timeframe after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="562d8dc1-7081-489f-9ac5-c3774de62cee">
  <data key="d3">The initiation of a new two-year contestability period depends on first satisfying reinstatement requirements, including providing proof of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="976d21fc-a08c-4c4a-994c-c5ac61731c42">
  <data key="d3">The start of a new two-year suicide and contestability period after reinstatement depends on having fulfilled the prerequisite condition of repaying delinquent premiums with 6% interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="6c3f8840-4647-406b-9929-e1b67417fe7f">
  <data key="d3">The initiation of a new two-year contestability period after reinstatement presupposes that the insured was alive at the time of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="c1512491-2648-4091-bf70-f69ea67b0895">
  <data key="d3">A new two-year contestability period begins at reinstatement, aligning with the resetting of the ROP calculation. This ensures consistency in policy terms when coverage resumes after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">COINCIDES_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes a condition triggered by policy reinstatement—the start of a new two-year suicide and contestability period. This does not influence or explain why the policy has a higher cost compared to standard term life insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating an ROP policy restarts key protections such as the suicide exclusion window, ensuring the original benefit structure remains intact despite lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="9a6c8495-0658-4de0-97a4-d8a49c0fec55">
  <data key="d3">While the policy has a 20-year term, reinstating it after a lapse restarts critical safeguards like the suicide clause, meaning these protections apply anew regardless of the initial term length.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_TERM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restarts key protections like the contestability period, but does not reset the original ROP timeline unless explicitly stated; thus, surviving the full term remains essential for premium recovery.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="d3dbbdfc-8830-4d2b-9fb8-abe4fce9331c">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses and is later reinstated, the new two-year contestability period restarts, potentially affecting whether the $32,400 in premiums would still be eligible for return under the ROP clause, especially if the insured dies during this newly activated period despite having previously met coverage requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">The return of premiums benefit depends on surviving the entire term without triggering exclusion clauses; therefore, any reinstatement triggers a new contestability period that could jeopardize the right to receive the $32,400 return if suicide occurs within two years post-reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy restarts key protections such as the two-year suicide clause, meaning that while the eventual return of premium remains possible, it becomes conditional on avoiding suicide during the newly activated contestability phase after reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="5093abc8-a7d6-401e-907e-6b80f82d69d2">
  <data key="d3">The rule about restarting the suicide and contestability period after reinstatement adds critical limitations to the 20-year term’s protection, meaning surviving the entire term does not automatically guarantee immunity from scrutiny if the policy was previously lapsed and revived.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="256028e2-0a3d-4e1d-8382-ed239b45e913">
  <data key="d3">If the policy is reinstated prior to September 15, 2044, it triggers a new two-year contestability period, directly affecting the enforceability of benefits at the policy’s final expiry.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="3cd53960-22e5-4307-8561-6aa1ffcfc09a">
  <data key="d3">The rule that a new two-year suicide and contestability period begins upon reinstatement affects the long-term implications of maintaining the policy, particularly regarding when benefits may become payable. Since the initial premium was set at $1,620 annually, any lapse and subsequent reinstatement would require re-evaluation of these risks during the renewed contestability window.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="600fcc21-f2ed-4013-854a-d0230dd726f7">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement triggers a new contestability period, which affects claims eligibility regardless of prior payments like those made under the annual premium plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="be98658a-9431-48d1-9c48-8e2bbc8f9f5c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy triggers a new contestability period, which could impact whether claims—including those tied to return of premium—are honored, especially if the claim arises shortly after reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="b8941628-eb5b-462b-bb77-5e37980a9491">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement triggers a reset of key protections like the contestability period (fact_sentence_2), which may override earlier accumulated rights such as partial premium returns under the original timeline, especially relevant when considering surrender options before Year 5 (fact_sentence_1).</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="2291fcf7-1262-4d16-a497-fd39b8260cc2">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restarts the contestability clock, which might influence whether a surrender request made during Years 6–10 qualifies for the 30% ROP payment, especially if it occurs shortly after reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="37554481-a747-480f-b5ff-4064a09717c7">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy triggers a new contestability period, meaning any claim arising from suicide within two years of reinstatement would not be covered—even if the original policy had already passed earlier contestability windows. This affects the overall viability of claiming returns under the ROP provision mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="2be37f90-16b7-4751-a378-763a991ab252">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restarts the contestability clock, which may limit claims despite having accumulated significant ROP entitlements before lapse, especially if death occurs shortly after renewal.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="a1316d59-f834-4b94-bf99-e1e6f0fab4b9">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restarts key protections like the suicide clause, potentially preventing the full ROP payout even if the original 20-year timeline was nearly complete.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="7314500d-44bb-4471-85ef-f7159db5e8ec">
  <data key="d3">The condition for receiving the full return of premiums depends on uninterrupted payment history, but reinstatement after lapse resets key protections like the contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="fc446cb8-cff7-4839-af40-f8f635e80d6d">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy initiates a fresh contestability period, which may affect claims related to death from suicide, but does not alter the penalty imposed on late payments regarding the return of premium benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="5f1f4076-64e8-474a-9882-b1eb76ae4168">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after a lapse activates a new two-year suicide and contestability period, yet any previous lapses still disqualify the policyholder from receiving the return-of-premium benefit unless all past obligations were met before lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4" target="119358df-e2ac-44bd-93c0-290a863c3911">
  <data key="d3">The rules governing cash value access in fact_sentence_1 depend on continuous premium payments and timing; reinstatement after lapse—as mentioned in fact_sentence_2—can disrupt these requirements, potentially voiding the return-of-premium benefit even if future payments are made.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bc16d76f-8448-44a5-9406-1b6528e0fc16" target="06dca34d-1332-47ca-87cb-7fe487dab3a4">
