<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="817d0dcb-1390-42ee-b441-ff53e6769ad8">
  <data key="d3">The higher cost of the ROP policy compared to standard term life insurance is explained by its return-of-premium feature, which guarantees a refund if no claim occurs during the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="a1786028-dc71-4811-9ab3-5b1cf40851d9">
  <data key="d3">The increased cost of the ROP policy stems from its refundable premium feature, while the non-taxability of the ROP payout ensures favorable post-maturity outcomes for the policyholder.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030">
  <data key="d3">The higher cost of the ROP policy stems from features like guaranteed premium refunds, and one contributing factor is that it lacks cash value accumulation, distinguishing it from permanent policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS_REASON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="a2168b6b-4681-4af8-b045-535c522d4bf7">
  <data key="d3">The increased cost of the policy compared to standard term insurance does not influence its lack of accumulated cash value, which is an inherent feature stated directly in the summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="a0b9d7b9-785c-4452-825e-f1e39198751f">
  <data key="d3">The higher cost of the ROP policy results from its unique refund feature, which makes seeking tax advice important since the returned amount isn't taxed but could still influence overall financial strategy.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="592ee71a-ba3c-405e-860a-4d3784a89956">
  <data key="d3">The increased cost of the ROP policy compared to standard term policies is unrelated to adjustments in the death benefit caused by age misstatements. One concerns pricing, the other underwriting corrections.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438">
  <data key="d3">The higher cost of the ROP policy compared to standard term insurance reflects its unique benefits, such as premium refunds and flexible ownership options like changing beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f">
  <data key="d3">The higher cost of the ROP policy reflects added benefits like the ability to convert to permanent insurance, enhancing its overall value despite increased premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">The increased cost of the ROP policy reflects its unique benefits, such as the guarantee of premium repayment. This financial feature remains intact regardless of inaccuracies in reported age, ensuring consistent payout terms even if underwriting data was incorrect.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY MAINTAINED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="3a894b15-ff54-4713-9288-259b598b0942">
  <data key="d3">The higher cost of the ROP policy compared to standard term policies stems from its unique refund mechanism. This financial characteristic enables greater flexibility in ownership, such as assigning the policy as collateral.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9" target="42965392-459d-48d5-9a6b-4e35621611ae">
  <data key="d3">The higher cost of the ROP policy is unrelated to the requirement that policy changes be submitted in writing. One concerns financial pricing, the other operational procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
