<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy does not accumulate cash value, its design relies on alternative mechanisms—like premium refunds—to provide benefits, justifying its elevated price relative to basic term insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="817d0dcb-1390-42ee-b441-ff53e6769ad8">
  <data key="d3">The absence of cash value in the policy does not influence why the policy costs more than standard term insurance. Premiums are driven by the return-of-premium guarantee, not by cash value mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="a1786028-dc71-4811-9ab3-5b1cf40851d9">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy does not accumulate cash value, any benefits received at maturity are purely refunds of premiums paid, reinforcing why they are not classified as taxable income.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="a0b9d7b9-785c-4452-825e-f1e39198751f">
  <data key="d3">The absence of cash value accumulation does not influence the necessity of seeking tax advice regarding the ROP payout. These points pertain to separate characteristics of the policy’s design and implications.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="a2168b6b-4681-4af8-b045-535c522d4bf7">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy does not accumulate cash value, there is no asset base to serve as collateral for loans. This lack of cash value inherently prevents any borrowing activity during the policy’s term.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="592ee71a-ba3c-405e-860a-4d3784a89956">
  <data key="d3">The absence of cash value accumulation is unrelated to how age misstatements impact the death benefit. This statement focuses on policy structure, whereas the second addresses actuarial corrections during claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438">
  <data key="d3">The absence of cash value accumulation reflects the policy’s financial design, separate from the administrative flexibility granted to owners. This feature emphasizes its term-like nature without investment components.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">The absence of cash value accumulation is unrelated to how age misstatements affect the ROP payout. This statement focuses on financial structure, whereas the second concerns underwriting accuracy and benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="3a894b15-ff54-4713-9288-259b598b0942">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s lack of accumulated cash value means it functions purely as protection without savings components, allowing greater flexibility in ownership actions like assigning it as collateral.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f">
  <data key="d3">The absence of cash value makes this policy more straightforward and less complex, enabling greater flexibility like converting to permanent coverage without being constrained by built-up equity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="42965392-459d-48d5-9a6b-4e35621611ae">
  <data key="d3">The policy's lack of cash value reflects its structural simplicity, but this characteristic has no bearing on the written submission requirement for policy modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="a176a4ea-8eba-4f29-8ca6-99b1da801960">
  <data key="d3">The absence of cash value ensures that any payout upon surrender comes solely from the predefined ROP schedule, not from built-up reserves. This structural characteristic enables predictable returns without reliance on investment growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030" target="8bd5fad5-80a8-43a1-911c-847ab0530599">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes a core characteristic of the policy regarding financial growth potential. The second sentence offers administrative contact details, which do not relate to the policy's structural or financial attributes described earlier.</data>
