  <data key="d3">The inability to borrow against cash value reflects a limitation in liquidity options during the term, whereas the non-taxability of the ROP payout concerns post-maturity taxation. Neither fact influences the truth or existence of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
