<edge source="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af" target="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9">
  <data key="d3">Even though age misstatements may reduce the death benefit, the return of premiums is unaffected, maintaining the policy’s core financial promise despite potential underwriting discrepancies. This stability contributes to why the policy commands a higher price compared to standard term options.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY MAINTAINED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af" target="817d0dcb-1390-42ee-b441-ff53e6769ad8">
  <data key="d3">While the ROP amount remains unaffected by age misstatements, this independence does not explain why the policy costs more than standard term plans. The pricing difference stems from the guarantee of premium refunds, not underwriting accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af" target="a1786028-dc71-4811-9ab3-5b1cf40851d9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 confirms that an incorrect age declaration affects only the death benefit, leaving the ROP amount intact. This ensures consistency in the refund regardless of underwriting inaccuracies, separate from how the payout is taxed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
