  <data key="d3">Changing beneficiaries is an ongoing right available to policyholders regardless of when the policy was executed. This action is independent of the policy's initiation date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438" target="d54d1ec1-8ffe-4752-acff-b1c3d194bed4">
  <data key="d3">Changing beneficiaries is a policyholder right related to ownership control, while the signature by the company president pertains to administrative validation of the contract’s execution. These actions occur at different stages and involve distinct parties.</data>
