  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438" target="884ef424-e8e1-4bf5-bf91-395b93140734">
  <data key="d3">The provision enabling beneficiary changes complements the initial setup where multiple beneficiaries were designated, ensuring ongoing alignment with the policyholder’s intentions.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438" target="bc29191c-c670-4cf2-8605-a8b1f962fa5e">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries supports the long-term planning aspect implied by the return of premiums, allowing owners to align payout intentions with evolving personal circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438" target="76ec6ed4-6f6f-47dc-9640-e032dc95e13a">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 allows flexible beneficiary management, this feature has no impact on the fixed $32,400 return specified in fact_sentence_1 upon successful completion of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438" target="0ff7a95c-a146-4ec1-9ada-e9ee6ce46b31">
  <data key="d3">Changing beneficiaries allows customization of payout distribution over time, whereas converting to permanent insurance provides an alternative coverage path beyond the initial term. Each function supports distinct aspects of policy ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">The freedom to change beneficiaries anytime supports flexible estate planning but operates independently of the fixed $32,400 return-of-premium amount payable at term end.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438" target="1c93bad2-a530-4021-9ae6-510c48444611">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows changes to beneficiaries, meaning the current designation of Carlos Roberto Martinez as primary could potentially be altered, reflecting ongoing flexibility in beneficiary assignment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CHANGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438" target="f0614009-4ad3-4925-af16-fcdd6c7ce2a0">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries means that Sofia Isabella Martinez’s role as contingent beneficiary is not fixed and could be updated by the policyowner, regardless of her current designation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The right to change beneficiaries at any time does not influence the policy’s increased cost tied to the return-of-premium provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
