<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="091a133f-a666-4ce6-99e0-7b5f5c79b9f9">
  <data key="d3">The option to convert to permanent insurance adds value to the policy, justifying its higher price compared to standard term plans.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="817d0dcb-1390-42ee-b441-ff53e6769ad8">
  <data key="d3">The availability of conversion to permanent insurance reflects the policyholder’s retained control, which is consistent with the overall structure of the ROP policy despite its higher initial cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSISTENT_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="a1786028-dc71-4811-9ab3-5b1cf40851d9">
  <data key="d3">The option to convert to permanent insurance reflects policyholder flexibility, independent of whether the ROP payout is taxable.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="a0b9d7b9-785c-4452-825e-f1e39198751f">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence highlights an ownership right allowing conversion to permanent insurance. This feature is unrelated to the tax considerations mentioned in the first sentence, even though both pertain to policyholder benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_RIGHT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="e16dc95e-60ca-4799-8cb5-4bd24f5a1030">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance highlights one of the advantages of owning a non-cash-value policy, emphasizing control over long-term protection options.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="a2168b6b-4681-4af8-b045-535c522d4bf7">
  <data key="d3">Although the policy lacks cash value and thus prohibits loans, its convertible nature provides owners continued flexibility, offsetting the limitation by enabling future access to permanent coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPENSATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="592ee71a-ba3c-405e-860a-4d3784a89956">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance grants long-term flexibility and ownership control. This feature operates independently of any adjustments to the death benefit caused by age misstatements during application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="9d3d7a34-a79d-4b06-8284-d7e63952d8af">
  <data key="d3">Policyholders have the option to convert the ROP policy into permanent insurance, offering greater protection beyond the term period. This right operates independently of how the ROP amount is determined or impacted by demographic errors.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="7164e6d5-1695-4226-9fba-8a306539e438">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance provides long-term protection options, whereas changing beneficiaries ensures alignment with personal circumstances. Both actions reinforce the policyholder’s autonomy, even though one does not influence the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="1b1a0da7-9963-49f3-a1df-1866fbbcbd3d">
  <data key="d3"></data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="3a894b15-ff54-4713-9288-259b598b0942">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes the right to convert the policy into permanent insurance, while fact sentence 2 outlines the ability to use the policy as collateral. Both highlight different aspects of policyholder control over the insurance product.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_RIGHTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="42965392-459d-48d5-9a6b-4e35621611ae">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance requires formal documentation submitted to the insurer’s home office, ensuring proper processing and compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_PROCESSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="a176a4ea-8eba-4f29-8ca6-99b1da801960">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance provides flexibility in long-term planning, whereas surrendering the policy for a refund offers liquidity at maturity or earlier. Both options reflect the policyholder’s retained control over the policy's lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="30c413b9-f29a-412d-9500-c61ba888fa87">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance reflects a right held by the policyholder but has no apparent link to the provision of customer service by ValueGuard Life Insurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="8bd5fad5-80a8-43a1-911c-847ab0530599">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes a policyholder right related to converting coverage type. This has no apparent connection to the second sentence, which lists a customer service contact number unrelated to policy conversions or benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="3ab835d7-2bde-49c4-a065-28119c8ede23">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance reflects a key ownership right but has no bearing on where the policy was signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="d54d1ec1-8ffe-4752-acff-b1c3d194bed4">
  <data key="d3">The policyholder’s right to convert to permanent coverage has no bearing on the identity or role of the individual who signed the policy document.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="d3024663-242e-4383-9899-d111f47feee0">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert the policy to permanent insurance reflects a key ownership right but has no connection to when the policy was executed.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="75780d21-da26-475c-b202-9491455a9f36">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance offers a strategic alternative before the policy ends, potentially affecting future access to the $32,400 return, depending on when conversion takes place.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="1c93bad2-a530-4021-9ae6-510c48444611">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s convertibility allows the owner greater control over its evolution, potentially altering future claims scenarios—though the existing beneficiary, Carlos Roberto Martinez, would remain designated unless formally changed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="f0614009-4ad3-4925-af16-fcdd6c7ce2a0">
  <data key="d3">The option to convert the policy to permanent insurance underscores the policyholder’s authority over the contract, including decisions affecting beneficiary distributions such as changing beneficiaries before conversion.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="26eb58bb-69a2-4679-a8d8-19898359d93f" target="b4a16075-b6bb-4b9d-8614-8a4e078e9175">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance complements the policy’s high cost driven by the return-of-premium feature, offering an alternative path for long-term financial planning despite the increased initial expense.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
